window.SUBJECTS.push({"id":"bio","n":"Biology","tab":"Biology","w":"Cells and genetics, the human body, health, plants and the living world.","topics":[{"id":"cell","n":"Cell, Genetics and DNA","qs":[{"id":"q0037","q":"Turner’s syndrome results due to:","o":["gain of extra copy of Y chromosome in human males","loss of a Y chromosome in human males","gain of extra copy of X chromosome in human females","loss of an X chromosome in human females"],"a":3,"x":"Turner's syndrome (45, X0) is a female with one X chromosome missing: short stature, underdeveloped ovaries, sterility.","e":"Klinefelter's syndrome is the opposite case: a male with an extra X (47, XXY).","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0072","q":"Which of the following is NOT an example of aneuploidy?","o":["Addison’s disease","Down syndrome","Edwards syndrome","Patau syndrome"],"a":0,"x":"Aneuploidy is a missing or extra chromosome: Down (trisomy 21), Edwards (trisomy 18) and Patau (trisomy 13). Addison's disease is an adrenal hormone deficiency.","e":"Trisomy 21-18-13: Down, Edwards, Patau.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0160","q":"Which of the following is NOT a salient feature of genetic code?","o":["AUG has dual functions.","The code is nearly universal.","Some amino acids are coded by more than one codon.","The codon is quadruplet."],"a":3,"x":"The genetic code is a triplet: three bases make one codon. It is nearly universal and degenerate (several codons for one amino acid), and AUG both codes methionine and starts translation.","e":"64 codons in all: 61 code for amino acids, 3 are stop codons.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0181","q":"The approximate size of the human genome is about:","o":["3000 Mb","4000 Mb","5000 Mb","6000 Mb"],"a":0,"x":"The human genome has about 3.2 billion base pairs, which is about 3,000 Mb (megabases).","e":"The Human Genome Project finished its sequence in 2003; there are about 20,000 protein-coding genes.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0228","q":"The number of codons that code for 20 amino acids is:","o":["55","58","61","64"],"a":2,"x":"Of the 64 codons, 61 code for the 20 amino acids and 3 (UAA, UAG, UGA) are stop codons.","e":"AUG codes methionine and is also the start codon.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0232","q":"According to Mendel, the factor responsible for the inheritance of specific traits is _________.","o":["chromosomes","factors","DNA","genes"],"a":3,"x":"Mendel called the units of inheritance 'factors'; today they are called genes, a word coined by Johannsen in 1909.","e":"Mendel worked with garden peas and gave the laws of dominance, segregation and independent assortment.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S1"],"k":"Mendel's own word was 'factors'; DSSSB's key marks the modern term, genes."},{"id":"q0308","q":"By which process is the information in RNA used to make proteins?","o":["Replication","Mutation","Synthesis","Translation"],"a":3,"x":"Translation is the process in which the ribosome reads mRNA and builds a protein from its codons.","e":"The central dogma: DNA → (transcription) → RNA → (translation) → protein.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0349","q":"The process by which genetic information is copied from one strand of the DNA into RNA termed as _______.","o":["transcription","replication","mutation","translation"],"a":0,"x":"Transcription copies genetic information from one DNA strand into RNA; translation then uses the RNA to build protein.","e":"Replication copies DNA into DNA.","src":["ASO 21 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0390","q":"Which of the following represents an autosomal dominant trait in a representative pedigree analysis (e.g., myotonic dystrophy)?","o":["Trait skips generations and appears only in males","Trait affects only males and is passed from father to son","Trait appears in every generation and affects both sexes equally","Trait appears only in offspring of carrier mothers"],"a":2,"x":"An autosomal dominant trait shows up in every generation and affects males and females equally; one faulty copy is enough.","e":"Myotonic dystrophy and Huntington's disease are autosomal dominant.","src":["ASO 21 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0436","q":"Which of the following combinations is correct?","o":["Sickle-cell anaemia – mutation on chromosome 11","Thalassaemia – X-linked inherited disorder","Down syndrome – only 45 chromosomes","Haemophilia – Y-linked inherited disorder"],"a":0,"x":"Sickle-cell anaemia is caused by a mutation in the β-globin gene on chromosome 11. Thalassaemia is autosomal (not X-linked), Down syndrome has 47 chromosomes, and haemophilia is X-linked.","e":"In sickle-cell anaemia one amino acid changes: glutamic acid → valine.","src":["ASO 22 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q1601","q":"The dense circular body part in the center of a cell is known as:","o":["Cell Membrane","Nucleus","Cell Wall","Cell tissue"],"a":1,"x":"The nucleus is the dense, usually round body at the centre of a cell that controls its activities and holds the DNA.","e":"Robert Brown discovered the nucleus in 1831.","src":["Patwari 17 Sep 2022 S2"]},{"id":"q2599","q":"Which of the following pair is/are correct? I. Red blood cells – spherical shaped II. Muscle cells – spindle shaped","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"NCERT describes red blood cells as rounded (spherical) and muscle cells as spindle-shaped; nerve cells are long and branched.","e":"Shape suits function: spindle muscle cells contract.","src":["Junior Clerk 16 Nov 2021 S3"],"k":"Strictly, human red blood cells are biconcave discs; the key follows NCERT Class 8's simpler description."},{"id":"q2670","q":"Which of the following pair is/are correct? I. Prokaryotic cell – have single chromosome II. Eukaryotic cell – have more than one chromosome","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"A prokaryotic cell usually has a single circular chromosome in a nucleoid; a eukaryotic cell has more than one chromosome inside a nucleus.","e":"Prokaryote: no nuclear membrane.","src":["Junior Clerk 16 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4891","q":"Which of the following is NOT a chemical base of DNA?","o":["Adenine","Cytosine","Guanine","Uracil"],"a":3,"x":"DNA has adenine, guanine, cytosine and thymine; uracil replaces thymine in RNA.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 26 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5019","q":"Which part of the cell serves as the cell’s command centre, sending directions to the cell to grow, mature, divide, or die?","o":["Nucleus","Lysosomes","Mitochondria","Ribosomes"],"a":0,"x":"The nucleus is the cell's control centre; it holds the DNA and directs growth and division.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 26 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5182","q":"Which of the following is a network of long fibres that make up the cell’s structural framework?","o":["Cytoplasm","Ribosome","Lysosomes","Cytoskeleton"],"a":3,"x":"The cytoskeleton is the network of protein fibres that forms the cell's framework.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 27 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5403","q":"What is the name of a membrane-bound cell organelle that contains digestive enzymes?","o":["Nucleolus","Cytoplasmic organelles","Ribosome","Lysosome"],"a":3,"x":"Lysosomes are membrane-bound sacs of digestive enzymes, called the 'suicide bags' of the cell.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 29 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5404","q":"Who determined the double-helix structure of DNA?","o":["Marie and Pierre Curie","Antoine and Marie-Anne Lavoisier","Gerty Theresa and Carl Ferdinand","James Watson and Francis Crick"],"a":3,"x":"James Watson and Francis Crick proposed the double-helix structure of DNA in 1953.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 29 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5445","q":"Which of the following cell organelles generate most of the chemical energy needed to power the cell's biochemical reactions?","o":["Mitochondria","Lysosome","Ribosome","Cytoplasm"],"a":0,"x":"Mitochondria, the 'powerhouses of the cell', make most of its energy as ATP.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 29 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q10048","q":"Human Genome Project (HGP) was closely associated with the rapid development of a new area in biology called _____.","o":["Biomagnification","Bioaccumulation","Bioinformatics","Biodiversity"],"a":2,"x":"The Human Genome Project drove the rapid growth of bioinformatics.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S1"]},{"id":"q10062","q":"In the double-helix structure of human DNA, base Adenine forms two hydrogen bonds with which of the following bases to form a base-pair?","o":["Guanine","Cytosine","Thymine","Histone"],"a":2,"x":"In DNA, adenine pairs with thymine by two hydrogen bonds; guanine pairs with cytosine by three.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S1"]},{"id":"q9491","q":"Who was the first to identify DNA as an acidic substance present in the nucleus?","o":["Friedrich Meischer","Carl Linnaeus","Edward Jenner","Rosalind Franklin"],"a":0,"x":"Friedrich Miescher first identified DNA ('nuclein') as an acidic substance in the nucleus, in 1869.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 14 Jul 2024 S1"]},{"id":"q9000","q":"What main role does DNA play inside a cell?","o":["Controls the cell’s chemical reactions","Information source for making proteins","Controls the cell's movement","Helps in digestion of food inside the cell"],"a":1,"x":"DNA carries the genetic information used to make proteins.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9081","q":"What is commonly called the \"energy currency\" of the cell in plants?","o":["Deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA)","Adenosine diphosphate (ADP)","Adenosine triphosphate (ATP)","Ribonucleic acid (RNA)"],"a":2,"x":"ATP (adenosine triphosphate) is the energy currency of the cell.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9117","q":"DNA carries genetic information in the form of _____.","o":["Sugars","Fatty acids","Nitrogenous bases","Amino acids"],"a":2,"x":"DNA stores genetic information in the sequence of its nitrogenous bases (A, T, G, C).","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9146","q":"The characters that are passed from parents to offspring are governed by _____ .","o":["Nucleolus","Alleles","Chromatids","Genes"],"a":3,"x":"Characters passed from parents to offspring are controlled by genes.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9199","q":"In humans, a mother always contributes which chromosome to each of her children?","o":["Z only","X or Y","Y only","X only"],"a":3,"x":"A mother always passes on an X chromosome; the father's X or Y decides the child's sex.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9231","q":"Which phase of the cell cycle involves the division of the cell's cytoplasm?","o":["S phase","G1 phase","M phase","G2 phase"],"a":2,"x":"Division of the cytoplasm (cytokinesis) happens in the M (mitotic) phase.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9309","q":"Which of the following statements is true about plasmids?","o":["Plasmids are RNA fragments.","Plasmids are DNA fragments and found in bacteria.","Plasmids are found in mammalian cells.","Plasmids are DNA fragments and found in fungi."],"a":1,"x":"Plasmids are small circular DNA pieces found in bacteria, used as vectors in genetic engineering.","e":"","src":["MTS 24 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9346","q":"Which of the following did Robert Hook observe while discovering the cell?","o":["Cork","Pencil","Paintbrush","Rubber"],"a":0,"x":"Robert Hooke discovered cells in 1665 while looking at thin slices of cork.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9393","q":"If a father possesses type A blood and a mother possesses type B blood, what are the potential blood types for their offspring ?","o":["Only AB","Only A or B","Only O","A, B, AB, or O"],"a":3,"x":"A type A parent (AO) and a type B parent (BO) can have children with blood group A, B, AB or O.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9394","q":"During respiration, the six carbon molecule, glucose, breaks down into three carbon molecules called:","o":["Acetylene","Propane","Benzene","Pyruvate"],"a":3,"x":"In respiration, glucose (six carbons) is broken into two molecules of pyruvate (three carbons) in the cytoplasm.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q3810","q":"Which of the following is true about eukaryotic cell? I. Nuclear region is well defined. II. Nuclear region is surrounded by nuclear membrane. III. It has a single chromosome.","o":["I and II","II and III","I and III","I, II and III"],"a":0,"x":"A eukaryotic cell has a well-defined nucleus surrounded by a nuclear membrane and has more than one chromosome, so III is wrong.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 22 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q0894","q":"Which of the following requires energy in the form of ATP?","o":["Active transport","Passive transport","Facilitated transport","Simple diffusion"],"a":0,"x":"Active transport moves substances against their concentration gradient and needs energy as ATP (e.g. the sodium-potassium pump); passive, facilitated transport and diffusion need none.","e":"Uphill needs fuel; downhill is free.","src":["PRT 16 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q0998","q":"The last amino acid in a protein sequence is called the _______.","o":["N-terminal","Beta-end","C-terminal","Omega group"],"a":2,"x":"A protein chain runs from the N-terminal (free amino group, first amino acid) to the C-terminal (free carboxyl group, last amino acid).","e":"Ribosomes build proteins from the N-terminal towards the C-terminal.","src":["PRT 19 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q1093","q":"Forward genetics is especially useful for identifying __________.","o":["Structural DNA changes","Protein stability","Chromosome numbers","Genes that control phenotypic traits"],"a":3,"x":"Forward genetics starts from an observed trait (phenotype) and works back to find the genes responsible; reverse genetics starts from a gene.","e":"Forward: trait → gene. Reverse: gene → trait.","src":["PRT 23 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9802","q":"______ are a kind of waste disposal system of the cell.","o":["Ribosomes","Mitochondria","Lysosomes","Golgi apparatus"],"a":2,"x":"Lysosomes are the cell's waste disposal system (suicide bags).","e":"","src":["PRT 7 Mar 2022 S1"]},{"id":"q1370","q":"Hydrogen peroxide is broken down by the ______ enzyme.","o":["Catalase","Oxidoreductases","Lyases","Isomerases"],"a":0,"x":"The enzyme catalase breaks hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen (2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂), protecting cells from damage.","e":"The fizz when peroxide touches a cut is catalase at work.","src":["TGT 24 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q1530","q":"The biological process by which traits pass from one generation to the next is called __________.","o":["Heredity","Regeneration","Mutation","Transformation"],"a":0,"x":"Heredity is the passing of traits from parents to offspring through genes.","e":"Genetics is the study of heredity and variation; Mendel is its father.","src":["TGT 24 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q8008","q":"The cutting of DNA by restriction endonucleases results in the fragments of DNA. These fragments can be separated by which of the following techniques?","o":["Paper chromatography","Isoelectric focusing","UV-visible spectrophotometer","Gel electrophoresis"],"a":3,"x":"DNA fragments cut by restriction enzymes are separated by gel electrophoresis.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8009","q":"Restriction enzymes are isolated from ___________.","o":["fungi","bacteria","algae","virus"],"a":1,"x":"Restriction enzymes are obtained from bacteria.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8010","q":"_________ are the site of protein synthesis in a cell.","o":["Golgi body","Lysosomes","Ribosomes","Mitochondria"],"a":2,"x":"Ribosomes are the site of protein synthesis.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8011","q":"During which phase of mitosis are the chromosomes spread through the cytoplasm of the cell?","o":["Prophase","Metaphase","Anaphase","Telophase"],"a":1,"x":"NCERT describes metaphase as the stage when the nuclear envelope has disintegrated and the chromosomes are spread through the cytoplasm before aligning at the equator.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8767","q":"Hydrogen peroxide is decomposed by the enzymes ______.","o":["oxidoreductases","lyases","catalase","isomerases"],"a":2,"x":"The enzyme catalase breaks down hydrogen peroxide into water and oxygen.","e":"","src":["TGT 24 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8826","q":"What are the different forms of the same gene, which can result in variations such as eye colour or disease risk, called?","o":["Genomes","Chromosomes","Nucleotides","Alleles"],"a":3,"x":"Alleles are different forms of the same gene.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 26 Jun 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q8369","q":"Which of the following statements about cell is INCORRECT?","o":["Prokaryotic cells have no nucleus.","Prokaryotes generally reproduce by binary fission.","Eukaryotic cells include archaea, bacteria, and cyanobacteria.","The size of eukaryotic cells ranges between 10–100 µm in diameter."],"a":2,"x":"Archaea, bacteria and cyanobacteria are prokaryotes, not eukaryotes.","e":"","src":["PGT 3 Nov 2022"]},{"id":"q8386","q":"Which of the following is NOT a cell organelle?","o":["Ribosome","Lysosome","Microsome","Mitochondria"],"a":2,"x":"Microsomes are fragments of endoplasmic reticulum formed in the lab, not true cell organelles.","e":"","src":["PGT 5 Jul 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q8414","q":"Who among the following invented a staining technique known as the ‘black reaction’ to study neurons, in which he/they used a weak solution of silver nitrate that is particularly valuable in detecting the processes and the most delicate effects of cells?","o":["Singer and Nicolson","Camilio Golgi","Albert von Kolliker","Wilhelm Waldeyer"],"a":1,"x":"Camillo Golgi invented the silver-nitrate 'black reaction' stain for studying nerve cells.","e":"","src":["PGT 21 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q5674","q":"Which part of a cell is medium for chemical reaction?","o":["Nucleus","Cytoplasm","Microtubules","Cilia"],"a":1,"x":"The cytoplasm is the jelly-like fluid where most of the cell's chemical reactions happen.","e":"","src":["Driver 30 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q7401","q":"Which of the following statement is correct? I. Prokaryotic cells lack nuclear membrane. II. Plant cells have a number of small vacuoles.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":0,"x":"Prokaryotic cells lack a nuclear membrane; plant cells usually have one large vacuole, not many small ones.","e":"","src":["Physical Education Teacher 2 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q8250","q":"Which of the following is NOT one of the methods to transport small molecules (such as glucose, amino acids, water, mineral ions etc.) across the plasma membrane?","o":["Diffusion","Osmosis","Active transport","Endocytosis"],"a":3,"x":"Endocytosis takes in large particles by engulfing them; small molecules cross the membrane by diffusion, osmosis or active transport.","e":"","src":["Librarian 10 Jul 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q8579","q":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT about the nucleus of a cell?","o":["The nucleus is the control centre of the cell.","The nucleus determines how the cell will function, as well as the basic structure of that cell.","The nucleus is separated from the cytoplasm by a membrane called the nuclear membrane.","Threads of chromatin in the nucleus contain ribonucleic acid (RNA)."],"a":3,"x":"Chromatin in the nucleus contains DNA, not RNA.","e":"","src":["Shift Incharge 25 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8717","q":"Which of the following combinations regarding cell wall composition and its respective organism is INCORRECT?","o":["Peptidoglycan - Bacteria","Chitin - Insects","Pectin - Fungus","Cellulose - Plants"],"a":2,"x":"Fungal cell walls are made of chitin; pectin is found in plant cell walls.","e":"","src":["Tailor Master 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q9890","q":"The unit of heredity is __________________.","o":["chromosome","nucleus","gene","DNA"],"a":2,"x":"The gene is the unit of heredity.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant 27 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q9907","q":"Which genetic principle states that genes located on different chromosomes assort independently during gamete formation?","o":["Law of Independent Assortment","Law of Segregation","Law of Co-dominance","Law of Dominance"],"a":0,"x":"Mendel's law of independent assortment says genes on different chromosomes assort independently.","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer (Mechanical) 5 Oct 2025 S2"]}]},{"id":"human","n":"Human Body","qs":[{"id":"q0107","q":"What type of tissue is blood made up of?","o":["Epithelial","Muscular","Connective","Meristematic"],"a":2,"x":"Blood is a fluid connective tissue: plasma is its matrix and it carries red cells, white cells and platelets.","e":"Other connective tissues: bone, cartilage, tendon, ligament, adipose (fat).","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0156","q":"What is the number of neurons found in the human brain?","o":["~16 billion","~86 billion","~16 million","~86 million"],"a":1,"x":"The human brain has about 86 billion neurons.","e":"The cerebellum holds most of them, although the cerebrum is larger.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0187","q":"The respiratory rhythm is primarily regulated by the respiratory centre located in the _______.","o":["medulla region","cerebellum region","cerebrum region","hypothalamus region"],"a":0,"x":"The respiratory rhythm centre is in the medulla oblongata; the pneumotaxic centre in the pons fine-tunes it.","e":"The medulla also controls heartbeat, swallowing and vomiting.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0275","q":"What is the function of the epiglottis during swallowing?","o":["To moisten the air","To produce sound","To help in breathing","To prevent food from entering the larynx"],"a":3,"x":"The epiglottis is a flap that closes over the larynx when you swallow, so food goes into the oesophagus and not the windpipe.","e":"Food 'going down the wrong pipe' is what happens when it fails.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0386","q":"The hormone that regulates blood sugar levels in the human body is:","o":["TSH","Estrogen","Insulin","Thyroxine"],"a":2,"x":"Insulin, from the beta cells of the islets of Langerhans in the pancreas, lowers blood sugar; glucagon from alpha cells raises it.","e":"Too little insulin causes diabetes mellitus.","src":["ASO 21 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0479","q":"The approximate amount of CO2 s directly dissolved in plasma is:","o":["0-3%","5-10%","15-25%","40-60%"],"a":1,"x":"About 7% (5–10%) of carbon dioxide is carried dissolved in plasma; about 70% goes as bicarbonate and about 20–25% bound to haemoglobin.","e":"Carbonic anhydrase in red blood cells speeds up bicarbonate formation.","src":["ASO 27 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0610","q":"Which of these organs helps in the filtration of blood?","o":["Kidney","Lungs","Gallbladder","Larynx"],"a":0,"x":"The kidneys filter blood: nephrons remove urea and excess salt and water to form urine.","e":"Each kidney has about a million nephrons.","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q0690","q":"___________ is the chemical process in which different types of chemical reactions involved in controlling the living state of the cells in an organism.","o":["Metabolism","Respiration","Transportation","Reproduction"],"a":0,"x":"Metabolism is the sum of all chemical reactions that keep a cell or organism alive: anabolism builds molecules and catabolism breaks them down.","e":"Respiration is one catabolic process.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q0691","q":"The lens focuses light on the back of the eye. The back of the eye is known as _____________.","o":["cornea","iris","lens","retina"],"a":3,"x":"The lens focuses light on the retina at the back of the eye, where rods and cones turn light into signals to the brain.","e":"Rods handle dim light; cones handle colour.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1747","q":"Which part of blood contains hemoglobin?","o":["Red Blood Cells","Platelets","White Blood Cells","Plasma"],"a":0,"x":"Haemoglobin, the iron-containing protein that carries oxygen, is found in red blood cells.","e":"Platelets clot blood; WBCs fight infection; plasma is the liquid part.","src":["Junior Clerk 11 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1749","q":"Which of the following statement regarding stomach and digestion is correct? I. Pancreatic juice contains trypsin. II. Mucus protects inner lining of stomach from the action of the acid. III. Gastric glands are present in the walls of stomach.","o":["I and II","II and III","I and III","I, II and III"],"a":3,"x":"Pancreatic juice contains trypsin; mucus protects the stomach lining from hydrochloric acid; gastric glands are in the stomach wall. All three statements are correct.","e":"Gastric juice = HCl + pepsin + mucus.","src":["Junior Clerk 11 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1984","q":"Bile juice is secreated by ______.","o":["Large Intestine","Liver","Food pipe","Kidney"],"a":1,"x":"Bile is made by the liver and stored in the gall bladder; it emulsifies fats in the small intestine.","e":"Bile has no enzymes, only bile salts.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2030","q":"On an average, an adult human being at rest breathes in and out ______ times in a minute.","o":["10 – 12","15 – 18","20 – 22","12 – 14"],"a":1,"x":"A resting adult breathes about 15–18 times a minute; exercise raises the rate.","e":"Normal breathing rate: 15–18 per minute.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2074","q":"Which of the following is a type of epithelial tissue? I. Squamous II. Cuboidal III. Columnar IV. Glandular","o":["II and III","II, III and IV","I, II and III","I, II, III and IV"],"a":3,"x":"Epithelial tissues include squamous, cuboidal, columnar, ciliated and glandular epithelium, so all four are correct.","e":"Epithelium covers organs and lines cavities.","src":["Junior Clerk 13 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2396","q":"What is the joint that joins our neck with the head called?","o":["Ball and socket joints","Pivotal joints","Hinge joints","Fixed joints"],"a":1,"x":"The joint between the neck and head is a pivot joint, which lets the head turn side to side.","e":"Ball and socket: shoulder; hinge: elbow, knee; fixed: skull.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2398","q":"What is the normal body-temperature in terms of degree Centigrade?","o":["34","37","27","40"],"a":1,"x":"Normal human body temperature is about 37°C (98.6°F).","e":"Fever begins above about 37.5°C.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2399","q":"When a person gets injured, which of the following cells in the blood leads to the formation of a clot that plugs the cut?","o":["Red Blood Cells","White Blood Cells","Haemoglobin","Platelets"],"a":3,"x":"Platelets help blood clot at a wound, plugging the cut.","e":"RBC: oxygen; WBC: immunity; platelets: clotting.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2600","q":"Which of the following pair is/are correct? I. Inhalation – ribs move up and outward II. Exhalation – ribs move down and inward","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"When we inhale the ribs move up and outwards and the diaphragm moves down, enlarging the chest; when we exhale the ribs move down and inwards.","e":"Diaphragm down = breathe in.","src":["Junior Clerk 16 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2869","q":"Which of the following statement(s) is/are correct? I. Birds excrete uric acid in semi solid form. II. In plants, foods is transported by phloem.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"Birds excrete nitrogenous waste as semi-solid uric acid, which saves water; in plants, food is transported by phloem. Both are correct.","e":"","src":["Junior Clerk 17 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6148","q":"During inhalation process, the ribs moves __________________ and diaphragm moves __________________","o":["out, back","out, down","back, back","back, down"],"a":1,"x":"When we breathe in, the ribs move up and out and the diaphragm moves down, enlarging the chest cavity.","e":"","src":["Junior Clerk 9 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6203","q":"Which of the following statement regarding human eye is correct? I. Light enters the eye through cornea. II. Iris controls the size of pupil. III. Eye lens forms an errect real image of the object on the retina.","o":["I and II","II and III","I and III","I, II and III"],"a":0,"x":"Light enters through the cornea and the iris controls the pupil's size; the lens forms a real but inverted image on the retina.","e":"","src":["Junior Clerk 9 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q10093","q":"Which of the following is a hormone which regulates blood glucose level in the body?","o":["Pepsin","Trypsin","Insulin","Rennin"],"a":2,"x":"Insulin, from the pancreas, regulates blood glucose; pepsin, trypsin and rennin are enzymes.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q8955","q":"Which of the following is a key component of nervous tissue?","o":["Neuron","Nephron","Dendrite","Axon"],"a":0,"x":"Neurons (nerve cells) are the key component of nervous tissue.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9001","q":"What is the function of an enzyme?","o":["To accelerate chemical reactions","To transport substances","To provide energy","To store genetic information"],"a":0,"x":"Enzymes are biological catalysts that speed up chemical reactions.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9052","q":"The thin, delicate membrane that surrounds a skeletal muscle cell is termed as:","o":["Sarcomere","Capsule","Myofibril","Sarcolemma"],"a":3,"x":"The sarcolemma is the membrane around a skeletal muscle cell.","e":"","src":["MTS 5 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9084","q":"The hormone that controls overall body growth is produced by the ____________.","o":["Pancreas","Pituitary gland","Adrenal gland","Thyroid gland"],"a":1,"x":"Growth hormone, which controls body growth, is produced by the pituitary gland.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9160","q":"Which structure links muscles to bones to enable movement in the human body?","o":["Ligaments","Cartilage","Tendons","Nerves"],"a":2,"x":"Tendons connect muscles to bones; ligaments connect bones to bones.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9191","q":"Our body’s stress response is influenced by the _________________.","o":["adrenal glands","thyroid gland","pineal gland","pancreas"],"a":0,"x":"The adrenal glands produce adrenaline and cortisol, which drive the body's stress response.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9261","q":"The site where complete digestion of foods takes place is __________.","o":["Pancreas","Small intestine","Stomach","Large intestine"],"a":1,"x":"Digestion of food is completed in the small intestine.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9307","q":"The enzyme salivary amylase is secreted from:","o":["Mouth","Small Intestine","Liver","Stomach"],"a":0,"x":"Salivary amylase is secreted in the mouth by the salivary glands.","e":"","src":["MTS 24 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9317","q":"What is the primary function of the red blood cells (erythrocytes) in the human body?","o":["Fighting infections","Producing antibodies","Carrying oxygen","Blood clotting"],"a":2,"x":"Red blood cells carry oxygen, using haemoglobin.","e":"","src":["MTS 24 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9421","q":"The inactive proenzyme form of pepsin is known as ___________.","o":["amylase","pepsinogen","trypsin","lactase"],"a":1,"x":"Pepsin is secreted in an inactive form called pepsinogen.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9426","q":"In the human circulatory system, what is the function of platelets?","o":["Immune response","Blood clotting","Nutrient absorption","Oxygen transport"],"a":1,"x":"Platelets help blood to clot.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9431","q":"In the human alimentary canal, the hydrochloric acid creates an acidic medium that facilitates the action of the enzyme _______.","o":["pepsin","amylase","renin","trypsin"],"a":0,"x":"Hydrochloric acid in the stomach creates the acidic medium pepsin needs to work.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9464","q":"Which of the following types of cells is NOT spherical?","o":["Nerve cell","Blood cell","Ovum cell","Fat cell"],"a":0,"x":"Nerve cells are long and branched, not spherical.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9471","q":"The semi-fluidic digestive juice with incompletely digested food forms an acidic soup in the stomach known as:","o":["Micelle","Bolus","Chyme","Bile"],"a":2,"x":"The partly digested, acidic food in the stomach is called chyme.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9472","q":"Which of the following is the primary function of the small intestine in the digestive system?","o":["Storage of bile","Synthesis of digestive enzymes","Absorption of nutrients","Mechanical digestion of food"],"a":2,"x":"The main function of the small intestine is absorbing nutrients.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q3420","q":"______ fights with germs that may enter our body.","o":["Red Blood Cells","White Blood Cells","Plasma","Haemoglobin"],"a":1,"x":"White blood cells fight germs that enter the body; red blood cells carry oxygen.","e":"","src":["Store Keeper 19 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3458","q":"Which of the following pair is correct? I. Arteries – carry oxygen rich blood II. Veins – carry carbon dioxide rich blood","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"Arteries carry oxygen-rich blood from the heart and veins carry carbon-dioxide-rich blood back to it (NCERT Class 7). Exceptions: the pulmonary artery and pulmonary vein.","e":"","src":["Store Keeper 19 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3210","q":"Which of the following releases hydrochloric acid used in digestion?","o":["Liver","Gastric glands","Oesophagus","Pancreas"],"a":1,"x":"Gastric glands in the stomach wall release hydrochloric acid, pepsin and mucus.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 18 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4011","q":"Which of the following is not a part of the nose?","o":["Vestibule","Olfactory chamber","Mesethmoid Cartilage","Pharynx"],"a":3,"x":"The vestibule, olfactory chamber and mesethmoid cartilage are parts of the nose; the pharynx lies behind the nose and mouth.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 22 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q6354","q":"Which of the following pair is correct? I. Atrium – Upper chambers of heart II. Ventricles – Lower chambers of heart","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"The two upper chambers of the heart are the atria and the two lower chambers are the ventricles.","e":"","src":["Care Taker 8 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q1033","q":"The bond between oxygen and haemoglobin is _________.","o":["Ionic","Reversible","Permanent","Irreversible"],"a":1,"x":"Oxygen binds to haemoglobin reversibly: it attaches in the lungs, forming oxyhaemoglobin, and is released in the tissues.","e":"Carbon monoxide binds far more tightly, which is why it is poisonous.","src":["PRT 19 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q1106","q":"With the help of the enzyme carbonic anhydrase, how many molecules of H2CO3 can be produced per second?","o":["600,000","6,000","600","60,000"],"a":0,"x":"Carbonic anhydrase is one of the fastest enzymes: one molecule can form about 600,000 molecules of carbonic acid (H₂CO₃) per second from CO₂ and water.","e":"It is found in red blood cells and helps carry CO₂.","src":["PRT 23 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q1123","q":"The primary function of goblet cells in the intestines is to synthesise and secrete __________.","o":["Mucus","Hormone","Hydrochloric acid","Enzyme"],"a":0,"x":"Goblet cells in the intestinal lining make and release mucus, which lubricates and protects the gut wall.","e":"Named for their goblet (cup) shape.","src":["PRT 26 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q1449","q":"Glomerulonephritis are part of human ______ system.","o":["reproductive","respiratory","excretory","circulatory"],"a":2,"x":"Glomerulonephritis is inflammation of the glomeruli, the filtering units of the kidney, so it belongs to the excretory system.","e":"The glomerulus sits inside Bowman's capsule of the nephron.","src":["TGT 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q3355","q":"The dilation and constriction of pupils is due to the effect of ________ on the human body.","o":["Noise","Light","Pressure","Temperature"],"a":1,"x":"The pupil widens and narrows in response to light.","e":"","src":["TGT 18 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5728","q":"Which of the following is the largest artery in the human body?","o":["The subclavian artery","The femoral artery","The axilla","The aorta"],"a":3,"x":"The aorta is the largest artery in the human body.","e":"","src":["TGT 4 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5948","q":"Where is glycogen stored in the human body?","o":["Stomach","Gall Bladder","Liver","Kidney"],"a":2,"x":"Glycogen is stored mainly in the liver (and muscles).","e":"","src":["TGT 7 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q8006","q":"Which of the following enzymes helps in digestion of fats?","o":["Amylase","Trypsin","Pepsin","Lipase"],"a":3,"x":"Lipase digests fats; amylase acts on starch and trypsin and pepsin on proteins.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8007","q":"Red blood cells (RBC) are formed in the _____________.","o":["bone marrow","spleen","pancreases","heart"],"a":0,"x":"Red blood cells are formed in the bone marrow.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8021","q":"Which of the following statements regarding the nervous system of humans is INCORRECT?","o":["The somatic nervous system consists of two types of nerves – cranial nerves and spinal nerves.","There are three sets of cranial nerves which either emanate from or reach different locations of the brain.","There are three types of cranial nerves – sensory, motor, and mixed.","There are thirty one sets of spinal nerves coming out of or reaching to the spinal cord."],"a":1,"x":"Humans have 12 pairs of cranial nerves, not three sets, so statement B is wrong; there are 31 pairs of spinal nerves.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q3043","q":"Which of the following hormone is secreted by thyroid Gland?","o":["Thyroxine","Aldosterone","Prolactin","Angiotensin"],"a":0,"x":"The thyroid gland secretes thyroxine.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 17 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q0818","q":"Which part of the human ear helps in the sensation of sound?","o":["Lungs","Semicircular canal","Retina","Cochlea"],"a":3,"x":"The cochlea, the snail-shaped part of the inner ear, turns sound vibrations into nerve signals for hearing. The semicircular canals handle balance.","e":"The auditory nerve carries these signals to the brain.","src":["PGT 22 Sep 2025"]},{"id":"q6636","q":"Which among the following statements is incorrect?","o":["The messages transmitted through the nervous system is in the form of electrical impulses which are known as nerve impulses.","The small gap between two neurons is called synapse.","There are 31 pairs of nerves that arise from spinal cord.","The short fibres coming out of the cell body of a neuron are called axon."],"a":3,"x":"The short fibres from a neuron's cell body are dendrites; the axon is the long fibre, so statement D is wrong.","e":"","src":["PGT 18 Jul 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q7081","q":"Which is the largest gland in the human body?","o":["Thyroid","Pituitary","Liver","Thymus"],"a":2,"x":"The liver is the largest gland in the human body.","e":"","src":["PGT 17 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7229","q":"______________ is the study of kidneys.","o":["Odontology","Neurology","Neonatology","Nephrology"],"a":3,"x":"Nephrology is the study of the kidneys.","e":"","src":["PGT 31 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7250","q":"________ is the process in which the absorbed food is taken in by the body cells and used for energy, growth and repair.","o":["Egestion","Ingestion","Assimilation","Absorption"],"a":2,"x":"Assimilation is the process in which absorbed food is used by body cells for energy, growth and repair.","e":"","src":["PGT 29 Jul 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1631","q":"The human heart beats about ______ per minute in an adult person.","o":["110 – 120","90 – 100","55 – 65","70 – 80"],"a":3,"x":"An adult human heart beats about 70–80 times a minute (about 72 on average).","e":"","src":["Senior Scientific Assistant (Lie-Detection) 10 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2251","q":"Human body works within the pH range of ______ to ______.","o":["6; 6.8","7; 7.8","8; 8.5","4; 5"],"a":1,"x":"The human body works within a pH range of about 7.0 to 7.8.","e":"","src":["Senior Scientific Assistant (Ballistics) 13 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3290","q":"Which of the following statement is CORRECT? I. In Myopia, the image of distant objects is focussed beyond the retina. II. In hypermetropia, the image of nearby objects is focussed before retina.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Both are wrong: in myopia the image forms in front of the retina, and in hypermetropia behind it.","e":"","src":["Senior Scientific Assistant (Document) 18 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3718","q":"Which of the following glands of the human body produces the insulin hormone?","o":["Pituitary","Pancreas","Parathyroid","Pineal"],"a":1,"x":"The pancreas produces insulin.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Production) 21 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3990","q":"Which of the following is required to digest the food in stomach? 1. Minerals 2. Enzymes","o":["Only 1","Only 2","Both 1 and 2","Neither 1 nor 2"],"a":1,"x":"Food in the stomach is digested by enzymes; minerals do not digest food.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Printing) 22 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5675","q":"Which part of the human body stores the bile juice that breaks down fats into fatty acids, which can be taken into the body by the digestive tract?","o":["Duodenum","Appendix","Spleen","Gall Bladder"],"a":3,"x":"Bile is made in the liver and stored in the gall bladder; it emulsifies fats.","e":"","src":["Driver 30 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q9905","q":"What are epithelial cells primarily responsible for?","o":["Generating and transmitting electrical impulses in the nervous system","Forming protective barriers and linings in tissues and organs","Producing antibodies to fight infections","Transporting water and nutrients throughout the body"],"a":1,"x":"Epithelial cells form protective linings and barriers in tissues and organs.","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer (Mechanical) 5 Oct 2025 S2"]}]},{"id":"health","n":"Nutrition and Diseases","qs":[{"id":"q0031","q":"Which of the following statements about vitamins is/are correct? Statement A: With the help of Vitamin B the body's cells are functioning properly. Vitamin B also helps the body convert food into energy. Statement B: Vitamin A is important for normal vision, the immune system, and reproduction. Statement C: Vitamin K helps the body absorb and retain iron and protein.","o":["Only A and C","Only B and C","Only A and B","A, B and C"],"a":2,"x":"A and B are correct. C is wrong: Vitamin K is needed for blood clotting. Absorbing iron is helped by Vitamin C.","e":"The K comes from the German 'Koagulation' — clotting.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0078","q":"Which groups of people are recommended zinc supplementation by World Health Organization (WHO) and United Nations International Children's Emergency Fund (UNICEF)?","o":["Low-income elderly persons","Children with severe malnutrition or diarrhoea","Non-lactating women","All children in low-income areas where stunting is common"],"a":1,"x":"WHO and UNICEF recommend zinc, with ORS, for children with diarrhoea, and for severely malnourished children, because zinc shortens the illness and helps recovery.","e":"Standard advice: ORS plus 10–14 days of zinc for childhood diarrhoea.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0237","q":"In the context of diet and nutrition, what is the full form of RDA?","o":["Regular Dietary Allowances","Recommended Dietary Allowances","Required Diet Amount","Routine Diet Amount"],"a":1,"x":"RDA means Recommended Dietary Allowances: the daily intake of nutrients enough for nearly all healthy people.","e":"In India, ICMR–NIN sets RDAs.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0426","q":"Which element is necessary for the formation of haemoglobin?","o":["Iron","Zinc","Calcium","Magnesium"],"a":0,"x":"Iron is needed to make haemoglobin, the oxygen-carrying pigment of red blood cells; lack of it causes anaemia.","e":"Good sources: green leafy vegetables, jaggery, liver; Vitamin C helps absorption.","src":["ASO 22 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0472","q":"Which of the following is NOT a primary source of simple carbohydrate?","o":["Milk","Potato","Wheat","Meat"],"a":3,"x":"Meat is mainly protein and fat; milk (lactose), potato (starch) and wheat (starch) supply carbohydrates.","e":"Simple carbohydrates: glucose, fructose, lactose, sucrose.","src":["ASO 27 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q1603","q":"A lack of iodine in food causes ______.","o":["Goitre","Fever","Malaria","Cancer"],"a":0,"x":"Iodine deficiency causes goitre (swelling of the thyroid), since iodine is needed to make thyroxine.","e":"India's iodised salt programme fights iodine deficiency.","src":["Patwari 17 Sep 2022 S2"]},{"id":"q0654","q":"What is the scientific name of Vitamin B6?","o":["Cobalamin","Pyridoxine","Calciferol","Phytomenadione"],"a":1,"x":"Vitamin B6 is pyridoxine.","e":"B1 thiamine, B2 riboflavin, B3 niacin, B12 cobalamin; D calciferol; K phylloquinone.","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q0694","q":"Rickets is caused due to the deficiency of which of the following vitamins?","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin E","Vitamin C","Vitamin D"],"a":3,"x":"Rickets, soft and bent bones in children, comes from Vitamin D deficiency; in adults it is osteomalacia.","e":"The skin makes Vitamin D in sunlight.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q0734","q":"Which one of the following describes the term \"hypochondria\"?","o":["Sleep with hallucinations","Excessive snoring","Daytime sleeping","Anxiety about state of health"],"a":3,"x":"Hypochondria (illness anxiety disorder) is excessive worry about having a serious illness despite little or no evidence.","e":"Insomnia is a sleep disorder; hallucinations are false perceptions.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6782","q":"Which among the following minerals is added to common salt to prevent goitre?","o":["Copper","Kynaite","Iron","Iodine"],"a":3,"x":"Iodine is added to common salt to prevent goitre.","e":"","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q1957","q":"Who introduced the first polio vaccine in the world?","o":["Alexander Fleming","Jonas Salk","Joseph E. Murray","Karl Landsteiner"],"a":1,"x":"Jonas Salk developed the first successful polio vaccine (injected inactivated virus) in 1955; Albert Sabin later made the oral vaccine.","e":"India was declared polio-free in 2014.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2442","q":"Which of the following is an example of a chronic disease?","o":["Common cold","Elephantiasis","Appendicitis","Influenza"],"a":1,"x":"A chronic disease lasts a long time. Elephantiasis (lymphatic filariasis) is chronic, while cold, flu and appendicitis are acute.","e":"Filariasis is spread by the Culex mosquito.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2488","q":"Which of the following category of micro-organisms do Leishmania fall under that causes kala-azar?","o":["Bacteria","Virus","Protozoa","Fungus"],"a":2,"x":"Kala-azar is caused by the protozoan Leishmania donovani, spread by the sandfly.","e":"Malaria (Plasmodium) is also protozoan.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2527","q":"Which of the following is responsible for peptic ulcers?","o":["Helicobacter pylori","Lactobacilus","Pseudomonas","Hay bacilus"],"a":0,"x":"Most peptic ulcers are caused by the bacterium Helicobacter pylori (Marshall and Warren, Nobel 2005).","e":"Lactobacillus turns milk into curd.","src":["Junior Clerk 16 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1299","q":"Which of the following foods has the highest percentage of proteins per unit mass?","o":["Egg","Meat","Cow-milk","Fish"],"a":1,"x":"Of these, meat has the highest protein per unit mass (about 25–30% in lean cooked meat), ahead of fish, eggs (about 13%) and milk (about 3.5%).","e":"Plant sources rich in protein: soybean (about 36–40%), pulses.","src":["Stenographer 19 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6956","q":"The scientific name of Vitamin K1 is _______________.","o":["Cobalamin","Riboflavin","Phytomenadione","Pyridoxine"],"a":2,"x":"Vitamin K1 is phylloquinone (phytomenadione).","e":"","src":["Stenographer 8 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7002","q":"__________ disease is caused by Plasmodium.","o":["Typhoid","Cholera","Measles","Malaria"],"a":3,"x":"Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium, spread by female Anopheles mosquitoes.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 14 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q5181","q":"Which of the following vitamins is helpful in blood clotting and wound healing?","o":["Vitamin E","Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin K"],"a":3,"x":"Vitamin K is needed for blood clotting.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 27 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q10061","q":"Which of the following cannot be digested by the human body?","o":["Cellulose","Proteins","Fats","Vitamins"],"a":0,"x":"Humans cannot digest cellulose; it acts as roughage.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S1"]},{"id":"q10086","q":"Who among the following developed the world’s first successful vaccine?","o":["Blaise Pascal","Alan Turing","Theodore Case","Edward Jenner"],"a":3,"x":"Edward Jenner developed the world's first successful vaccine, against smallpox, in 1796.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q10097","q":"Contaminated water and poor sanitation are NOT associated with the transmission of which of the following diseases?","o":["Hepatitis A","Diabetes","Polio","Typhoid"],"a":1,"x":"Diabetes is not spread by contaminated water or poor sanitation; hepatitis A, polio and typhoid are.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q4474","q":"Which of the following gives the highest amount of energy?","o":["Carbohydrates","Protein","Fat","Vitamins"],"a":2,"x":"Fat gives about 9 kcal per gram, more than carbohydrates or proteins (about 4 kcal per gram).","e":"","src":["Office Superintendent 24 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4485","q":"Riboflavin also known as ______.","o":["Vitamin B2","Vitamin D","Vitamin E","Vitamin B1"],"a":0,"x":"Riboflavin is vitamin B2; thiamine is vitamin B1.","e":"","src":["Office Superintendent 24 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q8879","q":"Which of the following nutrient categories primarily provides energy to the human body?","o":["Carbohydrates, fats, and proteins","Water and dietary fibers","Enzymes and hormones","Vitamins and minerals"],"a":0,"x":"Carbohydrates, fats and proteins provide energy; vitamins and minerals are protective foods.","e":"","src":["MTS 2 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q8891","q":"Umami, one of the five fundamental taste sensations, is found in which food?","o":["Boiled potatoes","Marmalade","Cured meats","Pickled dills"],"a":2,"x":"Umami (savoury taste) is found in foods rich in glutamates, such as cured meats, cheese and soy sauce.","e":"","src":["MTS 2 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q8968","q":"Which complex biological molecule is composed of a glycerol backbone and three fatty acid chains?","o":["Triglyceride","Phospholipid","Proteoglycan","Steroid"],"a":0,"x":"A triglyceride (fat) is made of a glycerol backbone and three fatty acid chains.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q8971","q":"Which of the following food products is the best natural source of niacin (B3), vitamin D and vitamin A?","o":["Carrots","Whole wheat bread","Almonds","Salmon"],"a":3,"x":"Oily fish such as salmon is a good natural source of niacin, vitamin D and vitamin A.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9034","q":"What is the role of antioxidants in maintaining health?","o":["It enhances blood clotting.","It stimulates allergic reactions.","It neutralizes free radicals.","It promotes inflammation."],"a":2,"x":"Antioxidants neutralise free radicals that damage cells.","e":"","src":["MTS 5 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9042","q":"What is the basic unit of proteins obtained on hydrolysis?","o":["Monosaccharides","Amino acids","Nucleotides","Fatty acids"],"a":1,"x":"Proteins break down into amino acids on hydrolysis.","e":"","src":["MTS 5 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9050","q":"Recommended Dietary Allowances are meant to:","o":["Cover the needs of almost all healthy individuals","Apply only to people with medical conditions","Reduce food intake","Increase consumption of processed foods"],"a":0,"x":"Recommended Dietary Allowances are set to cover the needs of almost all healthy people.","e":"","src":["MTS 5 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9159","q":"Which nutrient deficiencies can lead to difficulty seeing in low light?","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin B","Vitamin D"],"a":0,"x":"Lack of vitamin A causes night blindness.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9163","q":"Wheat flour is high and primary source of which nutrient?","o":["Fat","Vitamin C","Proteins","Carbohydrates"],"a":3,"x":"Wheat flour is mainly a source of carbohydrates.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9233","q":"Amla is a good source of ____________.","o":["Vitamin D","Plant protein","Vitamin C","Vitamin K"],"a":2,"x":"Amla (Indian gooseberry) is one of the richest sources of vitamin C.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9267","q":"What is the most important source of energy for mammals obtained from the digestion of starch?","o":["Lactose","Glucose","Fructose","Sucrose"],"a":1,"x":"Starch is digested to glucose, the main energy source for mammals.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9345","q":"Which of the following vitamins is synthesised from cholesterol?","o":["Vitamin B","Vitamin A","Vitamin D","Vitamin K"],"a":2,"x":"Vitamin D is made in the skin from a cholesterol derivative when exposed to sunlight.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9359","q":"Match the following with the right symptoms and select the correct option. A. Scurvy 1. Soft bones B. Anemia 2. Glands in neck swells-up C. Goiter 3. Low iron D. Rickets 4. Bleeding gums","o":["A-3, B-2, C-4, D-1","A-4, B-3, C-2, D-1","A-3, B-1, C-2, D-4","A-1, B-3, C-2, D-4"],"a":1,"x":"Scurvy – bleeding gums; anaemia – low iron; goitre – swollen neck gland; rickets – soft bones.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9383","q":"If the carbohydrates and fats in our diet are lower than the amounts required for our body, the ___________ present in our food is/are utilised to give us energy.","o":["water","vitamins","minerals","proteins"],"a":3,"x":"If carbohydrates and fats are too few, the body uses proteins for energy.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q3594","q":"Raw potato is a perfect sample for the test of presence of ______.","o":["Protein","Starch","Vitamin B12","Vitamin C"],"a":1,"x":"A raw potato turns blue-black with iodine solution, showing it has starch.","e":"Iodine test: blue-black = starch.","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3597","q":"Which of the following is NOT an example of Acute disease?","o":["Common Cold","Strep throat","High blood pressure","Flu"],"a":2,"x":"High blood pressure is a chronic disease; common cold, strep throat and flu are acute (short-lasting).","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3633","q":"Which of the following is a bacterial disease?","o":["COVID","Malaria","Typhoid","Influenza"],"a":2,"x":"Typhoid is a bacterial disease (Salmonella typhi); COVID-19 and influenza are viral and malaria is protozoan.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3670","q":"Which of the following body-organs is affected by Japanese Encephalitis?","o":["Bones","Kidneys","Brains","Heart"],"a":2,"x":"Japanese encephalitis is a viral disease that inflames the brain; it is spread by Culex mosquitoes.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2978","q":"Which of the following is a staphylococci?","o":["Bacteria","Virus","Protozoa","Fungi"],"a":0,"x":"Staphylococci are bacteria; 'staph' infections cause boils and food poisoning.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 17 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3213","q":"Which of the following multiply very slowly?","o":["Virus","Bacteria","Fungi","Worms"],"a":3,"x":"Viruses, bacteria and fungi multiply very fast, while worms multiply very slowly (NCERT Class 9, 'Why Do We Fall Ill').","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 18 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3256","q":"Which of the following diseases is not caused by virus?","o":["Malaria","Dengue","Common cold","Influenza"],"a":0,"x":"Malaria is caused by the protozoan Plasmodium, not a virus; dengue, the common cold and influenza are viral.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 18 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3915","q":"Which of the following are not lifestyle diseases?","o":["Hypertension","Cancer","Common cold","Stroke"],"a":2,"x":"The common cold is an infectious viral disease; hypertension, cancer and stroke are lifestyle diseases.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 22 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4339","q":"Necrosis can be defined as:","o":["death of cells or tissues in a living body due to injury or disease.","excess circulating neutrophils in an individual's body.","a kidney disease characterized by oedema and loss of protein from the plasma into urine.","an abnormal mass of tissues that forms when cells grow beyond normal rate."],"a":0,"x":"Necrosis is the death of cells or tissue in a living body due to injury or disease.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 24 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4547","q":"Which of the following is a genetic disease?","o":["Leprosy","Typhoid","Malaria","Haemophilia"],"a":3,"x":"Haemophilia is an inherited (genetic) disorder in which blood does not clot properly. Leprosy and typhoid are bacterial; malaria is protozoan.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 25 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4618","q":"All of the following foods are a rich source of Ascorbic acid, except _____________.","o":["oranges","strawberries","potatoes","beef"],"a":3,"x":"Oranges, strawberries and potatoes contain vitamin C (ascorbic acid); beef has almost none.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 25 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4077","q":"Which of the following diseases occurs due to the lack of Vitamin C in the diet?","o":["Scurvy","Osteoporosis","Goitre","Diabetes"],"a":0,"x":"Lack of vitamin C (ascorbic acid) causes scurvy, with bleeding gums.","e":"","src":["Jr. Telephone Operator 23 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4429","q":"Tomato products are rich sources of folate, potassium and ______","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Vitamin E"],"a":1,"x":"Tomatoes are rich in vitamin C, potassium and folate.","e":"","src":["Hindi Translator-cum-Assisstant 24 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q1053","q":"Which of the following is/are not classified as (a) nutrient(s)?","o":["Vitamins","Hormones","Proteins","Water"],"a":1,"x":"Hormones are chemical messengers made by the body; they are not nutrients. The six nutrient groups: carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals and water.","e":"Insulin, thyroxine and adrenaline are hormones.","src":["PRT 20 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q1281","q":"Which of the following is an incomplete protein (a protein source that does not contain all essential amino acids in sufficient amounts)?","o":["Pulses (dal)","Milk","Egg","Fish"],"a":0,"x":"Pulses (dal) are an incomplete protein: they lack enough of the amino acid methionine, which is why dal is eaten with rice or roti. Milk, eggs and fish are complete proteins.","e":"Dal + rice together give all essential amino acids.","src":["PRT 10 Apr 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q4513","q":"Which of the following doctors pioneered the Gamete Intrafallopian Transfer (GIFT) Technique?","o":["Dr. Indira Hinduja","Dr. Aditi Pant","Dr. Kamini A. Rao","Dr. Jayshree Mondkar"],"a":0,"x":"Dr Indira Hinduja pioneered the Gamete Intrafallopian Transfer (GIFT) technique.","e":"","src":["Nursery Teacher 24 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q7892","q":"Which of the following macronutrients does NOT yield calories?","o":["Carbohydrates","Water","Fat","Proteins"],"a":1,"x":"Water does not provide calories; carbohydrates, fats and proteins do.","e":"","src":["Nursery Teacher 24 Jun 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q7893","q":"Which mineral assists insulin in glucose metabolism?","o":["Selenium","Copper","Chromium","Manganese"],"a":2,"x":"Chromium helps insulin in glucose metabolism.","e":"","src":["Nursery Teacher 24 Jun 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q7930","q":"Which vitamin helps in red blood cell synthesis?","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin B12","Vitamin C","Vitamin D"],"a":1,"x":"Vitamin B12 is needed to make red blood cells; its lack causes pernicious anaemia.","e":"","src":["Nursery Teacher 24 Jun 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q1392","q":"Which of the following is NOT a sexually transmitted disease?","o":["AIDS","Amoebiasis","Gonorrhea","Syphilis"],"a":1,"x":"Amoebiasis (amoebic dysentery), caused by Entamoeba histolytica, spreads through contaminated food and water, not sexually. AIDS, gonorrhoea and syphilis are STDs.","e":"Houseflies act as mechanical carriers of amoebiasis.","src":["TGT 24 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q1411","q":"Which of the following is a vector borne disease?","o":["Diabetes","Breast Cancer","Covid-19","Malaria"],"a":3,"x":"Malaria is a vector-borne disease: the Plasmodium parasite is carried by the female Anopheles mosquito.","e":"Other vector-borne diseases: dengue and chikungunya (Aedes), kala-azar (sand fly).","src":["TGT 25 Jun 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q1426","q":"In which of the following diseases does a parasite develop in the red blood cells (RBCs) of humans?","o":["Covid-19","Avian influenza","Dengue","Malaria"],"a":3,"x":"In malaria the Plasmodium parasite multiplies inside human red blood cells, bursting them and causing cycles of fever.","e":"The parasite first multiplies in the liver.","src":["TGT 25 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q1478","q":"Which of the following is NOT a rich source of Vitamin A?","o":["Carrot","Mango","Amla","Papaya"],"a":2,"x":"Amla (Indian gooseberry) is famous for Vitamin C, not Vitamin A. Carrot, mango and papaya are rich in beta-carotene, which gives Vitamin A.","e":"Lack of Vitamin A causes night blindness.","src":["TGT 7 Feb 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q1498","q":"Which of the following diseases, usually caused by vitamin B1 deficiency, exhibits loss of muscle function or paralysis of lower limbs as common symptoms?","o":["Beri-beri","Scurvy","Pellagra","Pernicious anemia"],"a":0,"x":"Beri-beri, from Vitamin B1 (thiamine) deficiency, causes muscle weakness, nerve damage and even paralysis of the legs.","e":"Scurvy: Vitamin C. Pellagra: B3 (niacin). Pernicious anaemia: B12.","src":["TGT 29 Aug 2025"]},{"id":"q1513","q":"According to 2025 updates, what is the causative agent of Trachoma, the eye disease India has eliminated?","o":["Streptococcus pneumoniae","Chlamydia trachomatis","Neisseria gonorrhoeae","Escherichia coli"],"a":1,"x":"Trachoma is an eye infection caused by the bacterium Chlamydia trachomatis; repeated infection can cause blindness. WHO declared India free of trachoma as a public-health problem in 2024.","e":"It spreads through flies and contact with eye discharge.","src":["TGT 24 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q1898","q":"Who has discovered Insulin?","o":["Domagk","Finsen","Salk","Banting"],"a":3,"x":"Frederick Banting (with Charles Best) discovered insulin in 1921.","e":"","src":["TGT 11 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2201","q":"Selman Waksman discovered streptomycin from this bacterium, which proved an effective medicine against:","o":["Ebola virus","Asthma","HIV","Tuberculosis"],"a":3,"x":"Selman Waksman discovered the antibiotic streptomycin, the first effective drug against tuberculosis.","e":"","src":["TGT 13 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5075","q":"Prakhar drank contaminated water from a municipal tap. Which possible disease can he catch because of it?","o":["Cholera","Covid-19","Elephantiasis","Malaria"],"a":0,"x":"Contaminated water can spread cholera; malaria and elephantiasis are spread by mosquitoes.","e":"","src":["TGT 26 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5517","q":"Mainly which vitamin protects teeth?","o":["Vitamin D","Vitamin B12","Vitamin B6","Vitamin E"],"a":0,"x":"Vitamin D helps the body absorb calcium, which keeps teeth and bones strong.","e":"","src":["TGT 2 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5583","q":"Which one of the following is not a Vector-Borne Disease?","o":["Ebola virus","Dengue fever","Malaria","Lymphatic filariasis"],"a":0,"x":"Ebola spreads by contact with body fluids, not by a vector; dengue, malaria and lymphatic filariasis are spread by mosquitoes.","e":"","src":["TGT 2 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5604","q":"In infants, the therapy for the cure of diarrhoea includes:","o":["magnesium","cadmium","iron","zinc"],"a":3,"x":"Zinc supplements, along with ORS, are used to treat diarrhoea in infants.","e":"","src":["TGT 30 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5772","q":"Rama is suffering from Beri beri. What deficiency does she have?","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin B","Vitamin C","Vitamin K"],"a":1,"x":"Beriberi is caused by a lack of vitamin B1 (thiamine).","e":"","src":["TGT 5 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5990","q":"Vibrio cholerae is a ______ shaped pathogen.","o":["Rod","Spiral","Comma","Circular"],"a":2,"x":"Vibrio cholerae, which causes cholera, is a comma-shaped bacterium.","e":"","src":["TGT 8 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6078","q":"Apple seeds, when chewed and digested, releases which of the following toxins into the blood stream?","o":["Bisphenol-A","Mercury","Lectins","Cyanide"],"a":3,"x":"Chewed apple seeds release cyanide (from amygdalin).","e":"","src":["TGT 8 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q6238","q":"Which of the following diseases does not spread through the air?","o":["Common cold","Pneumonia","Tuberculosis","Cholera"],"a":3,"x":"Cholera spreads through contaminated food and water; common cold, pneumonia and tuberculosis spread through the air.","e":"","src":["TGT 9 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q7488","q":"Which organism causes rust of wheat?","o":["Bacteria","Protozoa","Virus","Fungi"],"a":3,"x":"Rust of wheat is a fungal disease.","e":"","src":["TGT 1 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7562","q":"The E2025 initiative launched by WHO is against which disease?","o":["Malaria","TB","Smallpox","Polio"],"a":0,"x":"WHO's E-2025 initiative aims to eliminate malaria from 25 countries by 2025.","e":"","src":["TGT 7 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7986","q":"Rickets and osteopenia disorders are due to shortage of:","o":["proteins and fats","iron and phosphate","vitamin A and zinc","vitamin D and calcium"],"a":3,"x":"Rickets and osteopenia are caused by a shortage of vitamin D and calcium.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q7992","q":"Which of the following is a water-soluble vitamin?","o":["Vitamin A","Vitamin C","Vitamin D","Vitamin K"],"a":1,"x":"Vitamin C is water-soluble; vitamins A, D, E and K are fat-soluble.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8038","q":"Which of the following is/are affected during Keratomalacia?","o":["Eyes","Heart","Skin","Lungs"],"a":0,"x":"Keratomalacia, caused by severe vitamin A deficiency, affects the eyes (cornea).","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8049","q":"Red Ribbon Express was a nationwide communication campaign for generating awareness about ____________.","o":["Goitre disease","Tuberculosis","COVID-19 virus","HIV/AIDS"],"a":3,"x":"The Red Ribbon Express was a train-based campaign to spread awareness about HIV/AIDS.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q9814","q":"Our body converts β-carotene into _____.","o":["vitamin K","vitamin A","vitamin E","vitamin C"],"a":1,"x":"The body converts β-carotene into vitamin A.","e":"","src":["TGT 23 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q3066","q":"Exocrine Pancreatic Insufficiency (EPI) is caused by lack of _________.","o":["Digestive enzymes","Vitamins","Minerals","Hemoglobin"],"a":0,"x":"Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency is caused by a lack of digestive enzymes from the pancreas.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 17 Oct 2021","Special Educator 17 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q7596","q":"_____________ is caused by damage to the adrenal glands which make hormones to control the body’s response to stress and balance body salt and water.","o":["Graves' Disease","Addison's disease","Cushing's Syndrome","Parkinson's Disease"],"a":1,"x":"Addison's disease is caused by damage to the adrenal glands.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 8 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q0847","q":"What is the full form of AIDS?","o":["Acquired Identity Deficiency Syndrome","Associated Immuno Deficiency Syndrome","Associated Identity Deficiency Syndrome","Acquired Immuno Deficiency Syndrome"],"a":3,"x":"AIDS stands for Acquired Immuno Deficiency Syndrome, caused by HIV, which destroys the CD4 helper T-cells of the immune system.","e":"World AIDS Day: 1 December. ELISA is the screening test.","src":["PGT 14 Jul 2025"]},{"id":"q0855","q":"Which demographic indicator showed an increase from NFHS-4 (2015–16) to NFHS-5 (2019–21)?","o":["Maternal Mortality Ratio (MMR)","Infant Mortality Rate (IMR)","Anaemia among women (15–49 years)","Total Fertility Rate (TFR)"],"a":2,"x":"NFHS-5 (2019–21) found anaemia among women aged 15–49 rose to about 57%, from 53% in NFHS-4; infant mortality and fertility fell.","e":"India's total fertility rate fell to 2.0, below replacement level.","src":["PGT 14 Jul 2025"]},{"id":"q0860","q":"Which of the following is a major mineral needed by the human body?","o":["Molybdenum","Selenium","Chromium","Potassium"],"a":3,"x":"Potassium is a major mineral (macromineral) the body needs in large amounts for nerve impulses, muscle contraction and fluid balance. Molybdenum, selenium and chromium are trace minerals.","e":"Other macrominerals: calcium, phosphorus, sodium, magnesium.","src":["PGT 14 Jul 2025"]},{"id":"q8125","q":"Which of the following BMI (Body Mass Index) is considered as healthy weight for adults?","o":["Below 18.5","18.5 – 24.9","25.0 – 29.9","30.0 and above"],"a":1,"x":"A BMI of 18.5–24.9 is considered a healthy weight for adults.","e":"","src":["PGT 21 Jun 2023 S1"]},{"id":"q8465","q":"Which of the following is NOT one of the components of AYUSH?","o":["Ayurveda","Homeopathy","Allopathy","Unani"],"a":2,"x":"AYUSH is Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homoeopathy; allopathy is not part of it.","e":"","src":["PGT 22 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8536","q":"1 g fat releases how much energy?","o":["4 cal","9 cal","4 Kcal","9 Kcal"],"a":3,"x":"One gram of fat gives about 9 kcal; carbohydrates and proteins give about 4 kcal.","e":"","src":["PGT 3 Nov 2022"]},{"id":"q8537","q":"Which of the following minerals makes the enamel of teeth hard and prevents dental caries?","o":["Fluoride","Chloride","Copper","Zinc"],"a":0,"x":"Fluoride hardens tooth enamel and helps prevent dental caries.","e":"","src":["PGT 3 Nov 2022"]},{"id":"q9856","q":"FSSAI is an autonomous body whose primary function is to protect and promote public health through the regulation and supervision of food safety. It is established by ____________.","o":["Government of India","United Nations","World Health Organization","UNICEF"],"a":0,"x":"FSSAI was set up by the Government of India under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.","e":"","src":["PGT 17 Jul 2025"]},{"id":"q2636","q":"The National Cancer Awareness Day is observed annually in India on ________ to spread awareness on cancer.","o":["September 2","October 21","November 7","August 21"],"a":2,"x":"National Cancer Awareness Day is observed on 7 November, Marie Curie's birth anniversary.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Interior Design) 16 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2792","q":"Which of the following is NOT a water-borne disease?","o":["Alzheimer's","Hepatitis A","Typhoid","Amoebiasis"],"a":0,"x":"Alzheimer's is not water-borne; hepatitis A, typhoid and amoebiasis are.","e":"","src":["Inspecting Officer 16 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2944","q":"Which of the following organs is affected mainly during jaundice?","o":["Heart","Liver","Lungs","Brain"],"a":1,"x":"Jaundice mainly affects the liver.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Intrumentation & Control) 17 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3499","q":"Helicobacter pylori is responsible for-","o":["Peptic ulcers","Typhoid","Malaria","Chicken Pox"],"a":0,"x":"Helicobacter pylori bacteria cause peptic ulcers.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant (Lie-Detection) 1 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3507","q":"Which of the following days was celebrated as the World Blood Donor Day 2021?","o":["12 June","14 June","16 June","18 June"],"a":1,"x":"World Blood Donor Day is observed on 14 June, Karl Landsteiner's birthday.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant (Lie-Detection) 1 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4115","q":"What is the common name of Myocardial infarction?","o":["Plague","Rabies","Leprosy","Heart Attack"],"a":3,"x":"Myocardial infarction is the medical name for a heart attack.","e":"","src":["Veterinary and Livestock Inspector 23 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4141","q":"Amino acids are largely found in:","o":["Carbohydrate","Protein","Fat","Vitamin"],"a":1,"x":"Proteins are made of amino acids.","e":"","src":["Manager (Public Relations) 23 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4218","q":"The most common cause of goitres worldwide is a lack of _______ in the diet.","o":["iron","potassium","sodium","iodine"],"a":3,"x":"Lack of iodine is the most common cause of goitre.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Civil) 23 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5054","q":"A food item turns blue-black when 2-3 drops of Iodine solution is added to it. It indicates the presence of which of the following in the food item?","o":["Protein","Fats","Starch","Fiber"],"a":2,"x":"Iodine turns blue-black when starch is present.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant (Physics) 26 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5055","q":"Which of the following causes kala-azar?","o":["Staphylococci","Leishmania","Trypanosoma","Roundworm"],"a":1,"x":"Kala-azar is caused by the protozoan Leishmania.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant (Physics) 26 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5099","q":"Which of the following is not an example of food rich in ‘Ascorbic Acid’?","o":["Amla","Vinegar","Orange","Lemon"],"a":1,"x":"Vinegar is acetic acid; amla, orange and lemon are rich in ascorbic acid (vitamin C).","e":"","src":["Laboratory Assistant (Photo) 26 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5118","q":"What is the scientific name of Vitamin D?","o":["Tocopherol","Calciferol","Thiamine","Riboflavin"],"a":1,"x":"Vitamin D is calciferol.","e":"","src":["Assistant Engineer (Civil) 26 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5249","q":"Night Blindness is caused by the severe deficiency of which of the following vitamins?","o":["Vitamin B","Vitamin A","Vitamin D","Vitamin C"],"a":1,"x":"Night blindness is caused by vitamin A deficiency.","e":"","src":["Assistant Engineer (Civil) 27 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5289","q":"What is the common name of Hansen's disease?","o":["Chicken pox","Rabies","Leprosy","Plague"],"a":2,"x":"Hansen's disease is leprosy.","e":"","src":["Assistant Engineer (Civil) 27 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5796","q":"Which among the following is a hormonal disease?","o":["Goitre","Malaria","Cholera","Rickets"],"a":0,"x":"Goitre is a hormonal (thyroid) disorder.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Electrical) 5 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5922","q":"Which of the following is the main cause for transmission of the 'Hepatitis C ' virus?","o":["Bite of Mosquito","Contaminated food","Sharing Drug Needle","Sharing Cloth"],"a":2,"x":"Hepatitis C spreads mainly through blood, such as shared drug needles.","e":"","src":["Laboratory Assistant (Chemistry) 7 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6291","q":"Heat treatment process that destroys pathogenic microorganisms in certain foods and beverages is called ______.","o":["Hydrolysis","Pasteurization","Solvay Process","Dehydrogenation"],"a":1,"x":"Pasteurisation is heat treatment that kills harmful microbes in food and drinks.","e":"","src":["Section Officer (Horticulture) 9 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6293","q":"Which of the following is a water-borne disease?","o":["Hepatitis A","Malaria","AIDS","Dengue"],"a":0,"x":"Hepatitis A is water-borne; malaria and dengue spread through mosquitoes and AIDS through body fluids.","e":"","src":["Section Officer (Horticulture) 9 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6427","q":"Which among the following pairs of disease and body part affected is wrong?","o":["Glaucoma - Eyes","Typhoid - Intestine","Otitis - Skin","Rickets - Bones"],"a":2,"x":"Otitis affects the ear, not the skin.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Digital Electronics) 7 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7032","q":"______________ is also known as Achromatopsia.","o":["Colour-blindness","Chicken pox","Mumps","Leprosy"],"a":0,"x":"Achromatopsia is complete colour blindness.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Medical Lab Technology) 1 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7463","q":"Which among the following vitamins is also known as ‘Folic Acid’?","o":["B3","B12","B7","B9"],"a":3,"x":"Folic acid is vitamin B9.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Pharmacy) 2 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q8163","q":"Which of the following is not an Antioxidants?","o":["Beta-carotene","Lutein","Globulin","Selenium"],"a":2,"x":"Globulin is a protein, not an antioxidant; beta-carotene, lutein and selenium are.","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer (Civil) or Section Officer (Civil) 27 Jun 2022 S2"]},{"id":"q8715","q":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT?","o":["Pulses are a rich source of protein.","Potato is a rich source of starch.","Citrus fruits are a rich source of vitamin E.","Wholegrains are a rich source of fibre."],"a":2,"x":"Citrus fruits are rich in vitamin C, not vitamin E.","e":"","src":["Tailor Master 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q8720","q":"Omega-3 fatty acids are good for our body because:","o":["they can control elevated triglyceride levels","they can increase triglyceride levels","they can lower the immune response","they can quickly activate inflammatory reactions"],"a":0,"x":"Omega-3 fatty acids help lower high triglyceride levels.","e":"","src":["Tailor Master 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q9883","q":"FSSAI is an autonomous body established for regulating and supervising the food safety standards in India. What does FSSAI stand for?","o":["Federal Standardization and Safety Authority of India","Food Security and Standards Authority of India","Food Safety and Standards Authority of India","Food and Safety Standards Authorization of India"],"a":2,"x":"FSSAI is the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant 27 Jul 2024 S2"]}]},{"id":"plants","n":"Plants","qs":[{"id":"q0071","q":"The plant tissue responsible for conduction of water and minerals is known as ________.","o":["xylem","lymph","chloroplast","cytoplasm"],"a":0,"x":"Xylem carries water and dissolved minerals up from the roots; phloem carries food made in the leaves.","e":"Xylem = water up; phloem = food around.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0120","q":"Identify the correct sequence from the outer to the inner side in the transverse section of a plant root.","o":["Epidermis – xylem – endodermis – pericycle – cortex","Epidermis – xylem – endodermis – cortex – pericycle","Epidermis – xylem – endodermis – pericycle","Epidermis – cortex – endodermis – pericycle – xylem"],"a":3,"x":"From outside in, a root cross-section shows epidermis, cortex, endodermis, pericycle, then the vascular tissue (xylem and phloem).","e":"Lateral roots grow from the pericycle.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0152","q":"The hormone auxin is primarily associated with _________.","o":["chlorophyll formation","seed storage","flowering in winter","cell elongation"],"a":3,"x":"Auxin causes cell elongation, which makes shoots bend towards light (phototropism); it also promotes rooting and apical dominance.","e":"Gibberellin: stem lengthening. Cytokinin: cell division. Abscisic acid: dormancy, the stress hormone. Ethylene: fruit ripening.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0186","q":"Which plant division is known for its unique reproductive structure called the 'cone'?","o":["Angiosperms","Pteridophyta","Bryophyta","Gymnosperms"],"a":3,"x":"Gymnosperms carry naked seeds on cones (strobili); pines, cycads and Ginkgo belong here.","e":"Angiosperms enclose seeds in fruits.","src":["ASO 19 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0262","q":"The primary pigment responsible for light absorption in photosynthesis is __________.","o":["Cobalamine","Chlorophyll","Plastocyanin","Carotenoids"],"a":1,"x":"Chlorophyll is the green pigment that absorbs light energy (mainly red and blue) for photosynthesis.","e":"Carotenoids are accessory pigments that protect chlorophyll.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0314","q":"What is the function of the ovary in a flower?","o":["Produce seeds","Support the anther","Produce pollen","Attract pollinators"],"a":0,"x":"The ovary holds the ovules. After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the ovary becomes the fruit, so the ovary is where seeds are produced.","e":"The anther makes pollen; petals attract pollinators.","src":["ASO 20 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0344","q":"Stolon that helps the plants in asexual reproduction is the modified form of the ____________.","o":["stem","root","leaf","bud"],"a":0,"x":"A stolon (runner) is a modified stem that grows along the ground and gives rise to new plants at its nodes.","e":"Examples: strawberry, grass. Potato tubers and ginger rhizomes are also modified stems.","src":["ASO 21 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q0350","q":"Which of the following is a major function of auxin in plants?","o":["Inhibiting seed growth","Promoting cell elongation","Promoting leaf fall","Stimulating root decay"],"a":1,"x":"Auxin's key job is promoting cell elongation, which drives shoot growth and bending towards light.","e":"Synthetic auxins such as 2,4-D are used as weedkillers.","src":["ASO 21 Aug 2025 S2"]},{"id":"q1622","q":"What is the botanical name of coffee plant?","o":["Coffea austinian","Coffea arabica","Coffea africanus","Coffea australiana"],"a":1,"x":"The main coffee plant is Coffea arabica (Arabica); Coffea canephora (Robusta) is the other major species.","e":"India mostly grows Arabica and Robusta in Karnataka, Kerala and Tamil Nadu.","src":["Patwari 20 Aug 2022 S2"]},{"id":"q0532","q":"Ferns belongs to which of the following divisions of the plant kingdom?","o":["Gymnosperms","Angiosperms","Thallophyta","Pteridophyta"],"a":3,"x":"Ferns belong to Pteridophyta, the first land plants with vascular tissue (xylem and phloem), which reproduce by spores.","e":"Other pteridophytes: horsetails (Equisetum), Selaginella, Marsilea.","src":["Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q0577","q":"The cultivation of trees and shrubs is known as _______________.","o":["Viticulture","Pomiculture","Arboriculture","Pisciculture"],"a":2,"x":"Arboriculture is the cultivation and care of trees and shrubs.","e":"Viticulture: grapes. Pomiculture: fruits. Pisciculture: fish.","src":["Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q0612","q":"Which among the plant kingdoms is also known as the amphibians of the plant kingdom?","o":["Bryophyte","Thallophyte","Gymnosperms","Angiosperms"],"a":0,"x":"Bryophytes (mosses, liverworts) are the 'amphibians of the plant kingdom': they live on land but need water for fertilisation.","e":"Examples: Funaria (moss), Marchantia (liverwort).","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q0732","q":"One of the following is classified as a flowering plant. Name it.","o":["Grasses","Conifers","Ferns","Mosses"],"a":0,"x":"Grasses are flowering plants (angiosperms, monocots). Conifers are gymnosperms, ferns are pteridophytes, and mosses are bryophytes.","e":"Wheat, rice, maize and bamboo are all grasses.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6780","q":"Chara belongs to which of the following plant kingdoms?","o":["Gymnosperms","Angiosperms","Thallophyta","Bryophyta"],"a":2,"x":"Chara is a green alga, so it belongs to Thallophyta.","e":"","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q1944","q":"Which of the following is not a simple tissue?","o":["Parenchyma","Collenchyma","Xylem","Sclerenchyma"],"a":2,"x":"Parenchyma, collenchyma and sclerenchyma are simple tissues (one cell type); xylem is a complex tissue made of several cell types.","e":"Complex tissues: xylem and phloem.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1945","q":"Which of the following pair of tissue – function is/are correct? I. Xylem – Water transport II. Phloem – Food transport","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"Xylem transports water and minerals; phloem transports food made in the leaves, so both pairs are correct.","e":"Xylem = water; phloem = food.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2075","q":"Which of the following is a vegetative part of a plant? I. Roots II. Stems III. Leaves IV. Flowers","o":["I, II and IV","III and IV","I, II and III","I, II, III and IV"],"a":2,"x":"Roots, stems and leaves are vegetative parts; flowers are reproductive parts.","e":"Vegetative propagation grows new plants from roots, stems or leaves.","src":["Junior Clerk 13 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2910","q":"Which of the following pair of tissue – type is correct? I. Parenchyma – Simple II. Xylem – Complex III. Sclerenchyma – Complex","o":["I and II","II and III","I and III","I, II and III"],"a":0,"x":"Parenchyma is a simple tissue and xylem a complex tissue; sclerenchyma is also simple (one cell type), so pair III is wrong.","e":"Simple: parenchyma, collenchyma, sclerenchyma; complex: xylem, phloem.","src":["Junior Clerk 17 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6201","q":"Which of the following is NOT a group of plant?","o":["Thallophytes","Protochordata","Bryophytes","Angiosperms"],"a":1,"x":"Thallophytes, bryophytes and angiosperms are plant groups; Protochordata is an animal group.","e":"","src":["Junior Clerk 9 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q1293","q":"What is the absorption of water by plant roots an example of?","o":["Photosynthesis","Endocytosis","Osmosis","Transplantation"],"a":2,"x":"Root hairs absorb water by osmosis: water moves from the dilute soil water into the more concentrated cell sap across a semi-permeable membrane.","e":"Minerals are taken up mostly by active transport, which uses energy.","src":["Stenographer 19 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1327","q":"The members of chlorophyceae are commonly called which of the following algaes?","o":["brown","red","blue","green"],"a":3,"x":"Chlorophyceae are green algae: their main pigments are chlorophyll a and b, and they store starch.","e":"Examples: Chlamydomonas, Spirogyra, Chlorella.","src":["Stenographer 23 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6859","q":"Plants growing on snow or ice are called as ___________.","o":["Epiphytes","Endophytes","Cryophytes","Thermophytes"],"a":2,"x":"Plants that grow on snow or ice are called cryophytes.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 14 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q6910","q":"Spirogyra reproduces through the process of ____________.","o":["fragmentation","regeneration","spore formation","budding"],"a":0,"x":"Spirogyra reproduces by fragmentation: its filament breaks into pieces that grow into new plants.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 14 Aug 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6999","q":"Rhizopus reproduces through the process of ____________.","o":["regeneration","fission","spore formation","fragmentation"],"a":2,"x":"Rhizopus (bread mould) reproduces by spore formation.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 14 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q4968","q":"The vascular tissue for the transport of water and nutrients in the plant is called the:","o":["phloem","collenchyma","xylem","sclerenchyma"],"a":2,"x":"Xylem carries water and minerals; phloem carries food.","e":"","src":["Personal Assistant 26 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q10056","q":"Which of the following algae rich in proteins is used as food supplements by space travellers?","o":["Dictyota","Fucus","Chlorella","Porphyra"],"a":2,"x":"The protein-rich green alga Chlorella is used as a food supplement, even by space travellers.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S1"]},{"id":"q10100","q":"Which of the following plants are those in which ovules are not enclosed by an ovary wall?","o":["Bryophytes","Gymnosperms","Pteridophytes","Angiosperms"],"a":1,"x":"In gymnosperms the ovules are not enclosed in an ovary (naked seeds).","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q10140","q":"Which of the following is a type of Brown algae?","o":["Volvox","Chlamydomonas","Laminaria","Spirogyra"],"a":2,"x":"Laminaria (kelp) is a brown alga; Volvox, Chlamydomonas and Spirogyra are green algae.","e":"","src":["Assistant Superintendent 20 Jul 2024 S3"]},{"id":"q8878","q":"In a plant, the absorption and upward movement of water and minerals dissolved in it from the roots to the leaves is due to the process of _________.","o":["Excretion","Transpiration","Respiration","Translocation"],"a":1,"x":"Transpiration from leaves creates a pull that draws water and dissolved minerals up from the roots.","e":"","src":["MTS 2 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q8888","q":"The curled top of a young fern frond is also commonly referred to as a/an:","o":["helix","fiddlehead","loop","obcordate"],"a":1,"x":"The curled tip of a young fern frond is called a fiddlehead.","e":"","src":["MTS 2 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q8921","q":"In which of the following options do all types of plant components belong to complex tissues?","o":["Sieve tubes, Tracheids, Companion cells, Aerenchyma and Collenchyma","Sclerenchyma, Tracheids, Companion cells, Phloem fibres and Chlorenchyma","Sieve tubes, Chlorenchyma, Companion cells, Phloem fibres and Xylem Parenchyma","Sieve tubes, Tracheids, Companion cells, Phloem fibres and Xylem Parenchyma"],"a":3,"x":"Sieve tubes, companion cells and phloem fibres (phloem), and tracheids and xylem parenchyma (xylem), are all parts of complex tissues.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q8928","q":"Which of the following hormones stimulates growth of the stem of a plant?","o":["Abscisic acid","Ethylene","Cytokinin","Auxin"],"a":3,"x":"Auxin promotes stem growth (cell elongation); abscisic acid inhibits growth.","e":"","src":["MTS 3 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9112","q":"What is the name of the small pores on leaves that control the exchange of gases?","o":["Cuticle","Stomata","Guard cells","Lenticels"],"a":1,"x":"Stomata are tiny pores on leaves that control gas exchange; guard cells open and close them.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9239","q":"Which factor accelerates the browning of bananas during the ripening process?","o":["The conversion of starch into protein.","The absorption of oxygen from the air.","The breakdown of sugar into starch.","The presence of ethylene gas."],"a":3,"x":"Ethylene gas speeds up ripening, including the browning of bananas.","e":"","src":["MTS 8 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9358","q":"Which of the following waste products are stored, especially in old xylem?","o":["Resins and Oxygen","Water and Carbon dioxide","Resins and Gums","Gums and Oxygen"],"a":2,"x":"Old xylem stores waste products such as resins and gums.","e":"","src":["MTS 25 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9437","q":"In mosses, spores are produced through _______.","o":["Binary fission","Mitosis","Budding","Meiosis"],"a":3,"x":"In mosses, spores are produced by meiosis.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9460","q":"What arrangement in plant tissues allows every cell to have contact with air?","o":["Cuticle layer","Vascular bundles","Large inter-cellular spaces","Thick cell walls"],"a":2,"x":"Large intercellular spaces in plant tissues let every cell be in contact with air.","e":"","src":["MTS 26 Feb 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q3671","q":"In which of the following group of plants is the plant-body differentiated into roots, stem and leaves and has specialised tissue for the conduction of water?","o":["Plantae","Thallophyta","Pteridophyta","Bryophyta"],"a":2,"x":"Pteridophytes (ferns) are the first plants with a body differentiated into root, stem and leaves and with vascular tissue for conducting water.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2712","q":"___________ are seed bearing, flowering vascular plants in which seeds are enclosed in fruits.","o":["Angiosperms","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms","Bryophytes"],"a":0,"x":"Angiosperms are flowering plants whose seeds are enclosed in fruits; gymnosperms have naked seeds.","e":"Angio = enclosed; gymno = naked.","src":["Ahlmad 16 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2828","q":"__________ are also called amphibians of the plant kingdom because these plants can live in soil but are dependent on water for sexual reproduction.","o":["Angiosperms","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms","Bryophytes"],"a":3,"x":"Bryophytes (mosses, liverworts) are called 'amphibians of the plant kingdom': they live on land but need water for sexual reproduction.","e":"","src":["Ahlmad 16 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3911","q":"Which of the following are commonly known as Brown Algae?","o":["Chlorophyceae","Phaeophyceae","Rhodophyceae","Bryophytes"],"a":1,"x":"Brown algae belong to class Phaeophyceae (e.g. kelps); green algae are Chlorophyceae and red algae Rhodophyceae.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 22 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4292","q":"How does Chlamydomonas reproduce?","o":["Fragmentation","Budding","Spore formation","Grafting"],"a":2,"x":"Chlamydomonas reproduces asexually by forming zoospores (spore formation).","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 24 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4546","q":"The Phloem in plants is responsible for which of the following functions?","o":["Conducting foods from leaves to all other parts of the plant.","Conducting water and dissolved minerals from roots to all parts of the plant.","Forming photosynthetic tissues in leaves.","Forming the supportive and protective layer over stems."],"a":0,"x":"Phloem carries food made in the leaves to other parts of the plant; xylem carries water and minerals up from the roots.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 25 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4078","q":"Mosses belong to which of the following plant kingdoms?","o":["Pteridophytes","Angiosperms","Bryophytes","Gymnosperms"],"a":2,"x":"Mosses belong to the Bryophytes, the 'amphibians of the plant kingdom'.","e":"","src":["Jr. Telephone Operator 23 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q1041","q":"Leaves characterized by parallel venation are a distinctive feature of:","o":["Gymnosperms","Monocots","Pteridophytes","Dicots"],"a":1,"x":"Parallel venation in leaves is typical of monocots, such as grasses, wheat, maize and banana. Dicots usually have net (reticulate) venation.","e":"Monocots also have fibrous roots and flower parts in threes.","src":["PRT 20 Feb 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q1058","q":"__________ is the outermost layer of the primary plant body.","o":["Epidermis","Endodermis","Hypodermis","Pericycle"],"a":0,"x":"The epidermis is the outermost layer of the primary plant body; it often has a waxy cuticle and stomata.","e":"Epidermis → cortex (incl. hypodermis, endodermis) → pericycle → vascular tissue.","src":["PRT 20 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q1545","q":"Agar is obtained from ______________.","o":["Aspergillus","Algae","Agaricus","Fungi"],"a":1,"x":"Agar is a jelly-like substance obtained from red algae such as Gelidium and Gracilaria, used in labs and food.","e":"Carrageenan also comes from red algae; algin from brown algae.","src":["TGT 31 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q1546","q":"Palm trees belong to which plant family?","o":["Arecaceae, a family of monocot flowering plants","Fabaceae, a family of leguminous flowering plants","Moraceae, a family of tropical flowering plants","Pinaceae, a family of coniferous evergreen plants"],"a":0,"x":"Palms belong to the Arecaceae family of monocot flowering plants.","e":"The coconut and the date palm are also Arecaceae.","src":["TGT 31 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q1710","q":"Which of the following items is known as Allium Cepa as its Botanical name?","o":["Brinjal","Onion","Potato","Tomato"],"a":1,"x":"Allium cepa is the botanical name of onion.","e":"","src":["TGT 10 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2304","q":"Which of the following statement is correct? I. Angiosperms are also called flowering plants. II. Pinus and Cycas are examples of Angiosperms.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":0,"x":"Angiosperms are flowering plants; Pinus and Cycas are gymnosperms, so only I is correct.","e":"","src":["TGT 13 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q8004","q":"Which of the following statements is INCORRECT?","o":["Turnip is a modification of root.","Ginger is a modification of root.","Potato is a modification of stem.","Sweet potato is a modification of root."],"a":1,"x":"Ginger is a modified stem (rhizome), not a root; turnip and sweet potato are modified roots and potato is a stem tuber.","e":"","src":["TGT 6 Jul 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q8795","q":"Plants that grow flowers and fruits belong to which group?","o":["Angiosperms","Gymnosperms","Ferns","Bryophytes"],"a":0,"x":"Angiosperms are flowering plants whose seeds are enclosed in fruits.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 24 Jun 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q8830","q":"Which of the following pigments in plants is essential for trapping light energy?","o":["Carotene","Xanthophyll","Anthocyanin","Chlorophyll"],"a":3,"x":"Chlorophyll traps light energy for photosynthesis.","e":"","src":["Special Educator 29 Jun 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q6568","q":"Which among the following belongs to Phanerogamia group?","o":["Thallophyta","Bryophyta","Pteridophyta","Angiosperm"],"a":3,"x":"Phanerogams are seed plants (gymnosperms and angiosperms); thallophytes, bryophytes and pteridophytes are cryptogams.","e":"","src":["PGT 3 Jul 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6635","q":"When a plant part shows directional movement in response to the touch of an object, it is called _____________.","o":["Thigmotropism","Hydrotropism","Geotropism","Phototropism"],"a":0,"x":"Movement of a plant part in response to touch is thigmotropism.","e":"","src":["PGT 18 Jul 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6660","q":"The botanical name of ____________ is Glycine max.","o":["soya bean","pea","groundnut","chickpea"],"a":0,"x":"Glycine max is the botanical name of soybean.","e":"","src":["PGT 10 Jul 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q7082","q":"Which of the following is a simple tissue? I. Xylem II. Phloem","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Xylem and phloem are complex tissues, so neither is a simple tissue.","e":"","src":["PGT 17 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7101","q":"Which gas is produced during photosynthesis?","o":["Nitrogen","Oxygen","Helium","Ozone"],"a":1,"x":"Photosynthesis releases oxygen.","e":"","src":["PGT 11 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7622","q":"What is the Scientific Name of the National Tree of India?","o":["The Banyan Tree","Fig Tree","Ficus bengalensis","Panthera Cristatus"],"a":2,"x":"The banyan, India's national tree, is Ficus benghalensis.","e":"","src":["PGT 17 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q9648","q":"Viticulture is known as the cultivation and harvesting of what?","o":["Grapes","Flowers","Wheat","Peanuts"],"a":0,"x":"Viticulture is growing grapes.","e":"","src":["PGT 29 Jun 2021"]},{"id":"q1673","q":"The phenomenon by which plant's growth is directed towards light is known as _________.","o":["Thigmotropism","Phototropism","Transpiration","Osmosis"],"a":1,"x":"Phototropism is plant growth directed towards light.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Computer) 10 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2230","q":"The out of a typical photosynthesis reaction where oxygen and carbon dioxide are combined is ______________.","o":["protein","glucose","starch","hydrogen carbonates"],"a":1,"x":"Photosynthesis uses carbon dioxide and water to make glucose, releasing oxygen.","e":"","src":["Laboratory Assistant (Lie Detection) 13 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3716","q":"Which of the following plants is from the Poppy family?","o":["Opium","Mustard","Barley","Maize"],"a":0,"x":"The opium plant belongs to the poppy family (Papaveraceae).","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Production) 21 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3720","q":"Which of the following is a gelatin-like product made primarily from red algae?","o":["Yeast","Agar-Agar","Mushroom","Euglena"],"a":1,"x":"Agar-agar, a gelatin-like substance, is made mainly from red algae.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Production) 21 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4171","q":"Which of the following bacteria lives in leguminous plants?","o":["Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Candida auris","Rhizobium","Acinetobacter baumannii"],"a":2,"x":"Rhizobium bacteria live in the root nodules of leguminous plants and fix nitrogen.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Automobiles) 23 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4176","q":"Which of the following plants has ‘hidden reproductive organs‘?","o":["Deodar","Cycas","Marsilea","Ipomoea"],"a":2,"x":"Marsilea, a fern (pteridophyte), is a cryptogam with hidden reproductive organs.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Automobiles) 23 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4253","q":"Phycology, the study of algae, is also known as:","o":["entomology","agrostology","algology","anemology"],"a":2,"x":"Phycology, the study of algae, is also called algology.","e":"","src":["Workshop Instructor 24 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4442","q":"In what form are carbohydrates stored in plants?","o":["Maltose","Lactose","Glucose","Starch"],"a":3,"x":"Plants store carbohydrates as starch.","e":"","src":["Laboratory Assistant (Documents) 24 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5119","q":"_________________ are called the amphibians of the plant kingdom.","o":["Bryophytes","Angiosperms","Pteridophytes","Gymnosperms"],"a":0,"x":"Bryophytes are called the amphibians of the plant kingdom.","e":"","src":["Assistant Engineer (Civil) 26 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q6002","q":"Which among the following plant kingdoms are divided into two - Monocots and Dicots?","o":["Thallophytes","Bryophytes","Angiosperms","Pteridophytes"],"a":2,"x":"Angiosperms are divided into monocots and dicots.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Electronic & Communication) 8 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q6707","q":"Which of the following is correct? I. Xylem transports food to all parts of plant. II. Phloem transports water and nutrients.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Both are wrong: xylem carries water and minerals, and phloem carries food.","e":"","src":["Investigator 26 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q8580","q":"Which of the following statements is correct about algae?","o":["Algae are chlorophyll-bearing, simple, thalloid, autotrophic and largely aquatic (both fresh water and marine) organisms.","Algae include the various mosses and liverworts that are found commonly growing in moist shaded areas in the hills.","Asexual reproduction in algae takes place by the fragmentation of thalli or by the formation of specialised structures called gemmae.","The predominant stage of the life cycle of algae is the gametophyte, which consists of two stages."],"a":0,"x":"Algae are chlorophyll-bearing, simple, thalloid, autotrophic and largely aquatic; mosses and liverworts are bryophytes.","e":"","src":["Shift Incharge 25 Jun 2023 S2"]},{"id":"q9716","q":"Identify the angiosperm among the following.","o":["Pinus","Cycas","Eucalyptus","Ginkgo"],"a":2,"x":"Eucalyptus is an angiosperm; Pinus, Cycas and Ginkgo are gymnosperms.","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer 29 Jun 2022 S3"]},{"id":"q9887","q":"The part of the tree that we call 'wood' is made up of _______________.","o":["xylem","chlorenchyma tissue","dermal tissue","cork"],"a":0,"x":"Wood is made of xylem.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant 27 Jul 2024 S2"]},{"id":"q9892","q":"In which of the following reactions is carbon dioxide reduced and water oxidised?","o":["Transpiration","Translocation","Photosynthesis","Glycolysis"],"a":2,"x":"In photosynthesis carbon dioxide is reduced and water is oxidised.","e":"","src":["Scientific Assistant 27 Jul 2024 S2"]}]},{"id":"living","n":"Classification and Animals","qs":[{"id":"q0118","q":"Identify the shape which is NOT found in the kingdom Monera.","o":["Bacilli","Vibrio","Cocci","Heterocyst"],"a":3,"x":"Bacteria (kingdom Monera) come in shapes such as cocci (round), bacilli (rods), vibrio (comma) and spirilla (spiral). A heterocyst is a nitrogen-fixing cell in some cyanobacteria, not a shape.","e":"Anabaena and Nostoc have heterocysts.","src":["ASO 18 Aug 2025 S3"]},{"id":"q0423","q":"Which of the following options correctly describes the term 'Thallophyta'?","o":["Plants that have large leaves","Plants that grow in colonies","Plants that are filamentous","Plants whose body is not well differentiated"],"a":3,"x":"Thallophyta are plants whose body is not differentiated into root, stem and leaves (a thallus), e.g. algae such as Spirogyra and Ulothrix.","e":"Thallus = undivided body.","src":["ASO 22 Aug 2025 S1"]},{"id":"q0494","q":"Earthworms belongs to which of the following phyla?","o":["Platyhelminthes","Annelida","Porifera","Arthropods"],"a":1,"x":"Earthworms belong to phylum Annelida: segmented worms with ring-like segments.","e":"Other annelids: leech, Nereis.","src":["Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q0570","q":"Bacteria belongs to which of the following Kingdoms?","o":["Plantae","Fungi","Protista","Monera"],"a":3,"x":"Bacteria belong to kingdom Monera in Whittaker's five-kingdom classification (1969): prokaryotes with no nuclear membrane.","e":"The five kingdoms: Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia.","src":["Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 21 Aug 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q0652","q":"Starfish belongs to which of the following phyla?","o":["Echinodermata","Platyhelminthes","Annelida","Porifera"],"a":0,"x":"Starfish belong to phylum Echinodermata: spiny-skinned marine animals with a water vascular system and tube feet.","e":"Other echinoderms: sea urchin, sea cucumber, brittle star. Despite the name, a starfish is not a fish.","src":["Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 25 Aug 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q0693","q":"Parrot belongs to which of the following classes of vertebrates?","o":["Reptilla","Amphibia","Aves","Pisces"],"a":2,"x":"Parrots belong to class Aves (birds): feathered, warm-blooded vertebrates that lay eggs.","e":"Other vertebrate classes: Pisces, Amphibia, Reptilia, Mammalia.","src":["Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021","Junior Assistant 31 Aug 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1792","q":"Which of the following is a characteristic of vertebrata? I. They have a notochord II. They are biploblastic III. They are coelomate","o":["I and II","II and III","I and III","I, II and III"],"a":2,"x":"Vertebrates have a notochord (at least in the embryo), are triploblastic (three germ layers, not diploblastic) and coelomate, so I and III are correct.","e":"Diploblastic = two layers, e.g. cnidarians.","src":["Junior Clerk 11 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q1986","q":"Which of the following pair is/are correct? I. Asexual reproduction – Fertilisation II. Sexual reproduction – Spore formation","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Fertilisation happens in sexual reproduction, and spore formation is asexual, so both pairs are wrong.","e":"Asexual: fission, budding, spores, fragmentation.","src":["Junior Clerk 12 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2111","q":"Which of the following is NOT an annelida? I. Leech II. Planaria III. Tape worm","o":["Only II","II and III","I and III","Only III"],"a":1,"x":"Planaria and tapeworm are flatworms (Platyhelminthes); the leech is an annelid (segmented worm).","e":"Annelids: earthworm, leech, Nereis.","src":["Junior Clerk 13 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2152","q":"Which of the following is not an example of Bryophyta?","o":["Riccia","Marchantia","Ulva","Funaria"],"a":2,"x":"Riccia, Marchantia and Funaria are bryophytes (liverworts and mosses); Ulva (sea lettuce) is a green alga.","e":"Bryophytes are the 'amphibians of the plant kingdom'.","src":["Junior Clerk 13 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2397","q":"With which of the following body-parts do redworms grind their food?","o":["Teeth","Gizzards","Gills","Claws"],"a":1,"x":"Redworms (earthworms) have no teeth; they grind food in their gizzard (NCERT Class 6).","e":"Birds also grind food in a gizzard.","src":["Junior Clerk 15 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q2598","q":"Which of the following is NOT Annelida?","o":["Nereis","Ascaris","Earthworm","Luch"],"a":1,"x":"Ascaris (roundworm) is a nematode (Aschelminthes); Nereis, earthworm and leech are annelids.","e":"Annelids are segmented.","src":["Junior Clerk 16 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2870","q":"Which of the following pair is/are correct? I. Hydra – Binary fission II. Amoeba – Budding","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Hydra reproduces by budding and Amoeba by binary fission, so both pairs are swapped and wrong.","e":"","src":["Junior Clerk 17 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1298","q":"Which of the following organism-classification does Anabaena belong to?","o":["Monera","Protista","Plantae","Fungi"],"a":0,"x":"Anabaena is a cyanobacterium (blue-green alga) and so belongs to kingdom Monera; it fixes nitrogen in its heterocysts.","e":"Anabaena lives with the water fern Azolla, used as a biofertiliser in rice fields.","src":["Stenographer 19 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1338","q":"Which among the following phyla is also known as sea walnuts?","o":["Ctenophora","Coelenterata","Platyhelminthes","Porifera"],"a":0,"x":"Ctenophores, the comb jellies, are called sea walnuts; they swim with eight rows of ciliated comb plates and show bioluminescence.","e":"Example: Pleurobrachia.","src":["Stenographer 23 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4045","q":"Aurelia is an example of which of the following phyla?","o":["Cnidaria","Ctenophora","Platyhelminthes","Aschelminthes"],"a":0,"x":"Aurelia (moon jellyfish) belongs to phylum Cnidaria (Coelenterata).","e":"","src":["Stenographer 23 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6862","q":"Commonly known forms of _____________ are mushrooms, bracket fungi or puffballs.","o":["phycomycetes","basidiomycetes","ascomycetes","deuteromycetes"],"a":1,"x":"Mushrooms, bracket fungi and puffballs belong to the basidiomycetes.","e":"","src":["Stenographer 14 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q8880","q":"An individual who came into being because of the fusion of a male and a female gamete is said to have been born because of _____.","o":["mitosis","asexual reproduction","sexual reproduction","binary fission"],"a":2,"x":"An individual formed by fusion of male and female gametes is produced by sexual reproduction.","e":"","src":["MTS 2 Mar 2026 S3"]},{"id":"q9087","q":"Some higher fungi produce a specific type of fruiting body that produces spores. These are called ______.","o":["Cone","Sporophore","Mycelium","Capsule"],"a":1,"x":"In higher fungi, the spore-producing fruiting body is called a sporophore.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S1"]},{"id":"q9119","q":"What is the term for a trait that is expressed even when only one copy of the gene is present?","o":["Homozygous","Dominant","Heterozygous","Recessive"],"a":1,"x":"A dominant trait shows even when only one copy of the gene is present.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q9121","q":"In Mendelian genetics, the presence of two dissimilar alleles for a particular trait, such as Rr in pea plants, is referred to as which condition?","o":["Heterozygous","Dominant","Homozygous","Monogenic"],"a":0,"x":"Two different alleles for a trait (such as Rr) is the heterozygous condition.","e":"","src":["MTS 6 Mar 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q3421","q":"Which of the following is unicellular? I. Amoeba II. Paramecium","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"Amoeba and Paramecium are both unicellular protists.","e":"","src":["Store Keeper 19 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3867","q":"Which among the following is an example of Arthropods phylum?","o":["Hydras","Starfish","Earthworms","Butterflies"],"a":3,"x":"Butterflies are arthropods (insects). Hydra is a cnidarian, the starfish an echinoderm and the earthworm an annelid.","e":"","src":["Store Keeper 22 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q3596","q":"Which of the following organism does NOT belong to the Monera kingdom?","o":["Bacteria","Rod-shaped Bacillus","Yeast","Cyanobacteria"],"a":2,"x":"Yeast is a fungus (kingdom Fungi), not Monera; bacteria, bacilli and cyanobacteria are Monera.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3635","q":"What are yeasts, molds, mushrooms examples of?","o":["Fungi","Protista","Monera","Plantae"],"a":0,"x":"Yeasts, moulds and mushrooms are fungi.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3636","q":"Which of the following are also known as sponges?","o":["Coelenterata","Platyhelminthes","Porifera","Nematode"],"a":2,"x":"Sponges belong to phylum Porifera, animals with pores all over the body.","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3673","q":"Which group of animalia are jellyfish and sea anemones common examples of?","o":["Coelenterata","Porifera","Annelida","Nematoda"],"a":0,"x":"Jellyfish and sea anemones belong to Coelenterata (Cnidaria).","e":"","src":["Fire Operator 20 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q2757","q":"Which among the following does not belong to phylum Aschelminthes?","o":["Round worm","Hook worm","Tape worm","Pin worm"],"a":2,"x":"The tapeworm is a flatworm (Platyhelminthes); roundworm, hookworm and pinworm belong to Aschelminthes (Nematoda).","e":"","src":["Ahlmad 16 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q4010","q":"Which gas is released when yeast begins to feed on sugars while making a bread dough?","o":["Carbon dioxide","Oxygen","Nitrogen","Carbon monoxide"],"a":0,"x":"Yeast ferments sugar and releases carbon dioxide, which makes bread dough rise.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 22 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4012","q":"Which of the following is an animal tissue?","o":["Vascular tissue","Epithelial tissue","Dermal tissue","Ground tissue"],"a":1,"x":"Epithelial tissue is an animal tissue; vascular, dermal and ground tissues are plant tissues.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 22 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4380","q":"This is a product of fermenting milk with the help of Lactobacillus bulgaricus and Streptococcus thermophilus.","o":["Butter","Yoghurt","Cottage Cheese","Butter milk"],"a":1,"x":"Yoghurt is made by fermenting milk with Lactobacillus bulgaricus and Streptococcus thermophilus.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 24 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q4382","q":"___________ ferments lactose sugar of milk to lactic acid.","o":["Lactobacillus","Staphylococcus","Leuconostoc","Streptococcus"],"a":0,"x":"Lactobacillus (lactic acid bacteria) converts milk sugar lactose into lactic acid, turning milk into curd.","e":"","src":["Fee Collector Sub Inspector Auction Recorder 24 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q1069","q":"Which of the following phyla does NOT show segmentation?","o":["Chordata","Mollusca","Annelida","Arthropoda"],"a":1,"x":"Molluscs (snails, octopus) are unsegmented soft-bodied animals. Annelids and arthropods are clearly segmented, and chordates show segmentation in muscles and vertebrae.","e":"Earthworm = segmented; snail = not.","src":["PRT 20 Feb 2026 S2"]},{"id":"q1491","q":"Which of the following is NOT among the five-kingdom classification proposed by R.H. Whittaker?","o":["Monera","Fungi","Xylem","Protista"],"a":2,"x":"R.H. Whittaker's five kingdoms (1969) are Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae and Animalia. Xylem is a plant tissue.","e":"MPFPA: Monera, Protista, Fungi, Plantae, Animalia.","src":["TGT 29 Aug 2025"]},{"id":"q4702","q":"In Amoeba, food is digested in a ______.","o":["Food vacuoles","Mitochondria","Endoplasmic reticulum","Plastid"],"a":0,"x":"In Amoeba, food is digested inside a food vacuole.","e":"","src":["TGT 25 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5202","q":"The mode of nutrition found in mushrooms is ______.","o":["Parasitic","Symbiotic","Saprophytic","Holozoic"],"a":2,"x":"Mushrooms are saprophytes: they feed on dead and decaying matter.","e":"","src":["TGT 27 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q5773","q":"Which of the following is a characteristic feature of Phylum – Chordata?","o":["Anterior proboscis","Collar","Long trunk","Pharyngeal gill slits"],"a":3,"x":"Pharyngeal gill slits (at some stage of life) are a key feature of phylum Chordata.","e":"","src":["TGT 5 Sep 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q6304","q":"Which of the following is NOT a fish?","o":["Mandarian fish","Lion fish","Jelly fish","Dog fish"],"a":2,"x":"The jellyfish is a cnidarian, not a fish; mandarin fish, lionfish and dogfish are fishes.","e":"","src":["TGT 9 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q7553","q":"Earthworms breathe through their ______.","o":["skin","lungs","gills","eyes"],"a":0,"x":"Earthworms breathe through their moist skin.","e":"","src":["TGT 7 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q0766","q":"Which of the following bacteria shows a 'Chinese letter' arrangement of cells?","o":["Clostridium tetani","Mycobacterium tuberculosis","Corynebacterium diphtheriae","Bacillus anthracis"],"a":2,"x":"Corynebacterium diphtheriae, which causes diphtheria, is seen under the microscope in a 'Chinese letter' arrangement of rod-shaped cells.","e":"Diphtheria is prevented by the DPT vaccine.","src":["PGT 25 Sep 2025"]},{"id":"q6493","q":"All single-celled eukaryotes are placed under which of the following kingdoms?","o":["Animalia","Monera","Protista","Fungi"],"a":2,"x":"All single-celled eukaryotes are placed in kingdom Protista.","e":"","src":["PGT 23 Jul 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q7060","q":"Which of the following pair is correct? I. Amoeba – Protozoa II. Bread Mold – Fungus","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":2,"x":"Amoeba is a protozoan and bread mould is a fungus, so both pairs are correct.","e":"","src":["PGT 11 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7102","q":"Which of the following pair of reproduction is correct? I. Asexual reproduction – Budding II. Sexual reproduction – Fragmentation","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":0,"x":"Budding and fragmentation are both asexual reproduction, so only I is correct.","e":"","src":["PGT 11 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q7159","q":"Mussels belong to which of the following phylum?","o":["Mollusca","Arthropoda","Aschelminthes","Annelida"],"a":0,"x":"Mussels are molluscs (phylum Mollusca).","e":"","src":["PGT 31 Jul 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q7274","q":"What is the Scientific Name of National Bird of India?","o":["Pavo Cristatus","Panthera Tigris","Peacock","Peak Cokoo"],"a":0,"x":"The Indian peafowl (national bird) is Pavo cristatus.","e":"","src":["PGT 10 Jul 2021"]},{"id":"q9521","q":"Cucumaria and Asterias belongs to which of the following Phyla?","o":["Mollusca","Echinodermata","Annelida","Arthropoda"],"a":1,"x":"Cucumaria (sea cucumber) and Asterias (starfish) belong to the phylum Echinodermata.","e":"","src":["PGT 30 Jun 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2578","q":"If an organism can nourish itself by making its own food using sunlight or chemicals such mode of nutrition is called as ______ nutrition.","o":["Holozoic","Heterotrophic","Autotrophic","Parasitic"],"a":2,"x":"Organisms that make their own food have autotrophic nutrition.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Medical Electronics) 16 Nov 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q2651","q":"Which of the following class of animals apart from mammals, maintain homeostasis?","o":["Reptiles","Fish","Birds","Amphibians"],"a":2,"x":"Besides mammals, birds are warm-blooded and keep a constant body temperature.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Interior Design) 16 Nov 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3334","q":"Which of the following statement is NOT correct? I. Cyclostomes are Jawless vertebrates. II. Arthropoda is the largest group of animals.","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":3,"x":"Both are correct: cyclostomes are jawless vertebrates, and Arthropoda is the largest animal phylum.","e":"","src":["Senior Scientific Assistant (Biology) 18 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q3721","q":"Human pinworm is an example of ______.","o":["bacteria","virus","aschelminthes","protozoans"],"a":2,"x":"The human pinworm is a roundworm (Aschelminthes).","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Production) 21 Oct 2021 S1"]},{"id":"q3991","q":"Which of the following animals do NOT have sweat glands?","o":["Whales","Horses","Rhinocerosos","Monkeys"],"a":0,"x":"Whales have no sweat glands.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Printing) 22 Nov 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4117","q":"Members of ___________ phylum are commonly known as sponges.","o":["Ctenophora","Platyhelminthes","Porifera","Coelenterata"],"a":2,"x":"Sponges belong to the phylum Porifera.","e":"","src":["Veterinary and Livestock Inspector 23 Apr 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4170","q":"Which of the following animals is from the Canidae family?","o":["Fox","Monkey","Crocodile","Lion"],"a":0,"x":"The fox belongs to the dog family, Canidae.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Automobiles) 23 Oct 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q4217","q":"Which of the following is the RIGHT sequence of the four stages in the metamorphosis of butterflies and moths?","o":["Egg, Pupa, Larva, and Adult","Egg, Larva, Pupa, and Adult","Egg, Cocoon, Pupa and Adult","Egg, Cocoon, Larva, and Adult"],"a":1,"x":"Butterflies and moths go through egg, larva, pupa and adult stages.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Civil) 23 Oct 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5120","q":"Snails belongs to ________ animal phylum.","o":["Anthropoda","Mollusca","Echinodermata","Platyhelminthes"],"a":1,"x":"Snails belong to the phylum Mollusca.","e":"","src":["Assistant Engineer (Civil) 26 Sep 2021 S3"]},{"id":"q5228","q":"Which of the following pair of animal – group is CORRECT? I. Jellyfish – Coelenterate II. Spider – Mollusca","o":["Only I","Only II","Both I and II","Neither I nor II"],"a":0,"x":"The jellyfish is a coelenterate, but the spider is an arthropod, not a mollusc.","e":"","src":["Senior Scientific Assistant (Chemistry) 27 Sep 2021 S2"]},{"id":"q5321","q":"Which among the following have highest average life span?","o":["Tiger","Human Being","Tortoise","Dog"],"a":2,"x":"Tortoises have the longest average lifespan of these.","e":"","src":["Laboratory Assistant (Biology) 28 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7419","q":"Which among the following is NOT an example of Diploblastic animals?","o":["Molluscs","Jellyfish","Corals","Sea Anemones"],"a":0,"x":"Molluscs are triploblastic; jellyfish, corals and sea anemones are diploblastic.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Fashion Design) 14 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q7464","q":"Which among the following animal kingdoms is also known as ‘comb jellies’?","o":["Ctenophora","Platyhelminthes","Aschelminthes","Annelida"],"a":0,"x":"Ctenophores are called comb jellies.","e":"","src":["Technical Assistant (Pharmacy) 2 Aug 2021"]},{"id":"q8198","q":"Which of these group has radial symmetry?","o":["Platyhelminthes","Porifera","Annelida","Cnidaria / Coelenterata"],"a":3,"x":"Cnidarians (coelenterates) have radial symmetry.","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer (Electrical) or Section Officer (Electrical) 22 Jun 2022 S1"]},{"id":"q8718","q":"Which of the following organisms is used by breweries for producing wine?","o":["Lactobacillus","Archaebacteria","Saccharomyces cerevisiae","Aspergillus"],"a":2,"x":"The yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae is used in brewing and winemaking.","e":"","src":["Tailor Master 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q8719","q":"Which of the following cells forms a temporary arm-like projection called pseudopodia for locomotion and ingestion of particles?","o":["Amoeba","Volvox","Spirogyra","Yeast"],"a":0,"x":"Amoeba moves and feeds using pseudopodia.","e":"","src":["Tailor Master 25 Jun 2023 S3"]},{"id":"q9749","q":"Polyp and Medusa body forms are found in _____.","o":["Phylum Mollusca","Phylum Echinodermata","Phylum Coelenterata (Cnidaria)","Phylum Ctenophora"],"a":2,"x":"Polyp and medusa body forms occur in Cnidaria (Coelenterata).","e":"","src":["Junior Engineer 28 Jun 2022 S3"]}]}]});
